trading options)\n5. Also the \"Area of Interest\" select — should probably only list Trading (or keep the departments for future?). Hmm — the user says strictly forex trading jobs. The area of interest select lists departments (Trading, Education, Marketing, Sales, Technology, Administration, Other). Should I trim that too? The jobs are only trading now, but interests could still be broad... Actually to be consistent with \"strictly forex trading jobs\", the form position list must be trimmed. The area of interest select — I could trim to Trading + Other, or leave it. Let me trim it to match: Trading, Other. Actually let me think — the \"coming soon\" card says sales/marketing/IT jobs are coming. So applicants interested in those departments could still join the talent pool. Keeping the full department list in \"Area of Interest\" is arguably fine for the talent pool form. But for the job application position select, only trading positions make sense.\n\nHmm, let me be sensible:\n- **Position Applying For** select: only the trading positions + \"General Application\" (maybe keep as option for talent pool-type applications). Actually since there are two forms, the job application should have trading positions only.\n- **Area of Interest** select (both forms): keep all departments since people can express interest in future departments (that's the point of the coming-soon card — signal interest). Actually, that's a nice synergy: the coming-soon card says sales/marketing/IT coming soon; candidates interested can note it in the form. Keep the departments in the interest select.\n- **Years of experience**: unchanged.\n\nAlso should I add MORE trading positions to replace the removed ones? The user said \"strictly forex trading jobs\" — the current 5 trading positions are good. I could add a couple more trading-specific ones (Senior Trader, Prop Trader, Market Research Analyst, Portfolio Analyst, Trade Support Specialist — from the original spec's trading department list