 Application).\n5. Add CSS for `.coming-soon` card.\n6. Update the hero? The hero says \"View Open Positions\" — fine. The Why Join section is generic — fine.\n\nAlso — the `data-position` values must match the select options. If I add new trading positions, add them to both the cards and the select.\n\nAlso the talent pool form's interest select — keep departments (future roles). Actually wait, let me reconsider: \"strictly forex trading jobs\" refers to the jobs posted. The interest select is about the applicant's interest — keeping it broad is fine and useful for the talent pool. Keep.\n\nAlso the Job Application form \"Area of Interest\" — for consistency, keep the same broad options (Trading, Education, Marketing, Sales, Technology, Administration, Other). Fine.\n\nHmm — but should the job application form's \"Area of Interest\" be trading-only? No — it's interest, keep broad.\n\nLet me plan the edits to careers.html:\n\nA. Remove these blocks (each department group):\n- Education group (Forex Instructor + Trading Coach)\n- Marketing group (Digital Marketing Specialist + Content Creator)\n- Sales group (Sales Consultant + Client Success Manager)\n- Technology group (Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, Data Analyst)\n- Administration group (Operations Manager, Virtual Assistant)\n\nB. Add 4 new trading cards after Junior Trader (or after Trading Mentor): Senior Trader, Prop Trader, Market Research Analyst, Trade Support Specialist. And update department-title comment (it's just \"Trading\").\n\nC. Add coming-soon card after the trading department-group (before </div></section> of positions).\n\nD. Update position select options: remove Education/Marketing/Sales/Technology/Administration positions, add the new trading ones.\n\nE. CSS: add `.coming-soon` styles.\n\nLet me do the removal efficiently with str_replace. Each department group is large. I'll remove each group by replacing from the comment `<!-- Education -->` through the end of that group (the closing `</div>` before `<!-- Marketing -->`).\n\nThis is fiddly with exact whitespace matching. Let me read the current careers.html positions section to get exact content... Actually I wrote the file, so I know the exact content. But safer to re-read the relevant section to get exact strings for replacement. The file is ~950 lines. Let me read the positions section (roughly lines 230-560 in current file — but line numbers shifted after nav edits? The nav edits added lines near top: +3 lines (nav li + mobile link + footer li = +3). So positions section starts around line 252+... let me just read the whole file sections.\n\nActually, rather than reading the whole file, let me use code_search to get the exact block boundaries. Hmm — the cleanest is to read the positions section of the file. Let me read careers.html but it's ~950 lines / large. read_files can handle it; the token limit is 20k — the file might exceed that. Let me read it in parts using code_searcher with context, or just read the file (it's mostly repetitive HTML; ~950 lines might be ~30-40k tokens — too big).\n\nBetter approach: use str_replace with the exact strings I wrote (I have them from my write_file content). The department groups are exactly as I wrote them. I know the exact text. Let me construct the replacements directly from what I wrote.\n\nThe Education group block (from my write):\n```\n      <!-- Education -->\n      <div class=\"department-group reveal\">\n        <h3 class=\"department-title\">Education</h3>\n        ... 2 job listings ...\n      </div>\n```\n\nI have the exact text from my write_file. Let me build str_replace calls removing each group, adding new trading cards, adding coming-soon, and updating the select.\n\nSince these are big blocks, str_replace with the full block as oldString is reliable. Let me be careful to reproduce exactly.\n\nActually, a smarter approach: replace the entire positions section content between the \"Trading\" group's end and the section close. Let me structure:\n\nThe section structure:\n```html\n      <!-- Trading -->\n      <div class=\"department-group reveal\">\n        <h3 class=\"department-title\">Trading</h3>\n        [5 job-listing blocks]\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Education -->\n      <div class=\"department-group reveal\">\n        ...\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Marketing -->\n      ...\n\n      <!-- Sales -->\n      ...\n\n      <!-- Technology -->\n      ...\n\n      <!-- Administration -->\n      ...\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n```\n\nPlan:\n1. Replace `<!-- Education -->` ... through the end of Administration group + closing `</div>` with:\n   - 4 new trading job listings (inside the Trading group, or as separate additions)\n   - coming-soon card\n   \nHmm, simpler: \n- Replace the Education-through-Administration blocks (everything between Trading group close and positions section close) with the new trading cards + coming-soon card.\n\nSo oldString = from `\\n      <!-- Education -->` to the end of the Administration group `      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>` — replace with new trading cards + coming-soon + section close.\n\nThat's one big replacement. The oldString would be ~250 lines. Doable but risky for exact match. Alternative: do it in smaller pieces:\n\nPiece 1: Remove Education group: oldString from `\\n      <!-- Education -->\\n      <div class=\"department-group reveal\">\\n        <h3 class=\"department-title\">Education</h3>\\n\\n        <div class=\"job-listing\">` ... hmm still large.\n\nLet me just do individual removals per department group with exact text from my write_file content. I have the full content I wrote. Each group is well-defined. Let me construct 5 removals (Education, Marketing, Sales, Technology, Administration) where oldString is the full group including trailing newline, and newString is empty.\n\nThen separately:\n- Add 4 new trading job listings after the Junior Trader block (inside Trading group).\n- Add coming-soon card after the Trading group close.\n- Update the select options.\n\nLet me get the exact strings from my write_file. I'll reconstruct them carefully.\n\nEducation group (exact from write):\n```\n      <!-- Education -->\n      <div class=\"department-group reveal\">\n        <h3 class=\"department-title\">Education</h3>\n\n        <div class=\"job-listing\">\n          <div class=\"job-head\">\n            <h3>Forex Instructor</h3>\n            <span class=\"job-badge\">Remote</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"job-meta\">\n            <span>Full-Time</span>\n            <span>Remote</span>\n            <span>2+ Years</span>\n            <span>Salary: R18,000 – R30,000 / mo</span>\n          </div>\n          <p>Deliver live lessons and structured curriculum across our academy tiers, from foundations to advanced\n            strategy.</p>\n          <ul class=\"job-requirements\">\n            <li>Deep Market Knowledge</li>\n            <li>Public Speaking</li>\n            <li>Curriculum Delivery</li>\n            <li>Patience &amp; Clarity</li>\n          </ul>\n          <a href=\"#apply\" class=\"btn btn-dark\" data-position=\"Forex Instructor\">Apply Now</a>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"job-listing\">\n          <div class=\"job-head\">\n            <h3>Trading Coach</h3>\n            <span class=\"job-badge\">Remote</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"job-meta\">\n            <span>Part-Time</span>\n            <span>Remote</span>\n            <span>1+ Year</span>\n            <span>Salary: R18,000 – R28,000 / mo</span>\n          </div>\n          <p>Work one-on-one with students to review their trading psychology, journaling, and execution habits.</p>\n          <ul class=\"job-requirements\">\n            <li>Coaching Experience</li>\n            <li>Psychology / Mindset</li>\n            <li>Trade Journaling</li>\n            <li>Empathy</li>\n          </ul>\n          <a href=\"#apply\" class=\"btn btn-dark\" data-position=\"Trading Coach\">Apply Now</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n```\n\nThis is long but exact. Doing 5 of these in one str_replace call is fine (multiple replacements).\n\nActually — a cleaner approach to avoid exact-match risk: use code_searcher to verify current content? I wrote the file and made only nav edits (which were near the top). The positions section is unchanged from my write. I'm confident in the exact content.\n\nLet me do it. I'll create the todo list first, then make the edits.\n\nNew trading positions to add (4):\n1. Senior Trader — Full-Time, Remote, 4+ Years, R35,000 – R55,000/mo. Desc: \"Execute larger book size, mentor juniors, and help refine the firm's core strategies.\" Skills: Advanced Price Action, Order Flow, Risk Management, Leadership.\n2. Prop Trader — Full-Time, Remote, 2+ Years, \"Funded — performance based\". Desc: \"Trade firm capital with defined risk parameters. Consistent performers earn scale-ups and revenue share.\" Skills: Proven Consistency, Risk Discipline, Emotional Control, MetaTrader.\n3. Market Research Analyst — Full-Time, Remote, 1+ Year, R18,000 – R28,000/mo. Desc: \"Research market trends, sentiment, and liquidity to support our analysts and mentors.\" Skills: Research, Data Gathering, Report Writing, Market Awareness.\n4. Trade Support Specialist — Full-Time, Remote, 1+ Year, R15,000 – R22,000/mo. Desc: \"Handle trade execution queries, platform troubleshooting, and client-facing support during market hours.\" Skills: MetaTrader, Customer Support, Problem Solving, Attention to Detail.\n\ndata-position values must match select options exactly: \"Senior Trader\", \"Prop Trader\", \"Market Research Analyst\", \"Trade Support Specialist\".\n\nNew select options for position (order): Technical Analyst, Fundamental Analyst, Risk Manager, Trading Mentor, Junior Trader, Senior Trader, Prop Trader, Market Research Analyst, Trade Support Specialist, General Application.\n\nSelect replacement: replace the current options list with the trimmed one.\n\nCurrent select options block:\n```html\n              <select id=\"position\" name=\"position\" required>\n                <option value=\"\" disabled selected>Select a position</option>\n                <option>Technical Analyst</option>\n                <option>Fundamental Analyst</option>\n                <option>Risk Manager</option>\n                <option>Trading Mentor</option>\n                <option>Junior Trader</option>\n                <option>Forex Instructor</option>\n                <option>Trading Coach</option>\n                <option>Digital Marketing Specialist</option>\n                <option>Content Creator</option>\n                <option>Sales Consultant</option>\n                <option>Client Success Manager</option>\n                <option>Frontend Developer</option>\n                <option>UI/UX Designer</option>\n                <option>Data Analyst</option>\n                <option>Operations Manager</option>\n                <option>Virtual Assistant</option>\n                <option>General Application</option>\n              </select>\n```\nNew:\n```html\n              <select id=\"position\" name=\"position\" required>\n                <option value=\"\" disabled selected>Select a position</option>\n                <option>Technical Analyst</option>\n                <option>Fundamental Analyst</option>\n                <option>Risk Manager</option>\n                <option>Trading Mentor</option>\n                <option>Junior Trader</option>\n                <option>Senior Trader</option>\n                <option>Prop Trader</option>\n                <option>Market Research Analyst</option>\n                <option>Trade Support Specialist</option>\n                <option>General Application</option>\n              </select>\n```\n\nComing soon card — add after the Trading department-group's closing `</div>` and before the positions section `</div>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>`. Actually the structure after Trading