value-card:hover::after {\n  opacity: 1;\n}\n\n.value-card:hover .value-number {\n  opacity: 1;\n  transform: translateY(-2px);\n}\n```\n\nThe `::after` with inset 0 would sit on top of content — need `pointer-events: none` and it would cover text visually with a transparent gradient — it's just a radial glow, mostly transparent, so text stays readable. But z-index: content should be above. Since ::after has no z-index, the ::after renders above the background but... actually pseudo-element ::after renders after the content? No — ::after is rendered as the last child, which is above other content in paint order unless z-index set. To be safe, keep the glow subtle (very low opacity) or use `z-index: 0` on it and `position: relative; z-index: 1` on the h3/p... Simpler: skip the ::after glow and use box-shadow glow on hover instead. And use ::before for the gold top line.\n\nAlso animate the value-number (color/opacity shift).\n\nLet me also add the hover to `.value-card h3` → gold color on hover. Nice touch.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```css\n.value-card {\n  position: relative;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.value-card::before {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  left: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 2px;\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent-gold), transparent);\n  opacity: 0;\n  transition: var(--transition);\n}\n\n.value-card:hover {\n  border-color: var(--accent-gold);\n  transform: translateY(-4px);\n  box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45), 0 0 28px rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.15);\n}\n\n.value-card:hover::before {\n  opacity: 1;\n}\n\n.value-card:hover .value-number {\n  opacity: 1;\n}\n\n.value-card:hover h3 {\n  color: var(--accent-gold);\n}\n\n.value-number {\n  transition: var(--transition);\n}\n```\n\nWait — the existing `.value-card:hover` rule already exists (border-color + translateY(-3px)). I'll replace it with the enhanced version and add the ::before + number/h3 transitions.\n\nNote: `.value-number` currently has `opaci