Replace with:\n   - A soft ambient gold glow behind the bull (`.hero-visual::before` — but it's currently `display:none` from \"Remove old glows\"). Re-enable with a classy breathing glow.\n   - Keep a very subtle mask or none.\n\n2. **Floating animation** — the bull gently floats (translateY ±10px, 6s ease-in-out infinite) — makes it feel alive.\n\n3. **Grounding shadow** — an elliptical shadow below that breathes opposite to the float (scale up when bull floats up) — makes it \"fit naturally\" on the page instead of floating detached.\n\n4. **Ambient breathing glow** — gold radial glow pulsing behind the bull.\n\n5. **Particles** — a few small gold dots drifting upward around the bull (like embers/sparks) for liveliness. CSS-only: use `.hero-visual` with extra spans? I'd need HTML elements. Alternatively use multiple box-shadows on a pseudo-element that animate. Let me add 3-4 small `<span class=\"spark\"></span>` elements to the HTML with staggered animations. That's clean.\n\n6. **Refine sweep** — keep the existing sweep but maybe soften/keep. The existing sweep is fine; keep it but ensure it's above the glow.\n\n7. **Bigger** — increase max-width to ~170% and max-height to ~92vh? Careful with overflow. The hero has overflow:hidden. The container is 90% width. hero-visual img max-width 150% already overflows the column (that's intended). Let me bump to 165% and 90vh, and reduce opacity slightly? Keep 0.55 or raise to 0.6.\n\nActually — since I can't see the screenshot, I need to be careful. Let me think about what \"cut out\" means: the radial mask fades the bull's edges to transparent, so on the flat black background, the bull appears as a floating vignetted image — like it's cut out and pasted. Making it \"fit naturally\": \n- Soften/remove the mask so the image blends with background\n- Add glow behind so it feels lit from within the scene\n- Add floor shadow to ground it\n- Float animation makes it alive\n\nBut removing the mask entirely might show harsh rectangular edges of the image (if the image itself has a background or hard edges). The mask was likely added to soften those edges. A middle ground: keep a very soft, wide mask (fade at 60% → transparent 90% instead of 30% → 70%) so edges barely fade.\n\nHmm — actually the image is a bull illustration on transparent background presumably (it's a PNG/webp of a bull). The mask might have been for aesthetic blending. Since the user says it looks \"cut out\", the mask is probably causing the issue. Let me soften it significantly.\n\nLet me design the CSS:\n\n```css\n/* ── Hero Bull — Bigger, Alive & Blended ── */\n.hero-visual {\n  position: relative;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n/* Soft ambient breathing glow behind the bull */\n.hero-visual::before {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 90%;\n  height: 90%;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background: radial-gradient(circle at center, rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.16), rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.05) 45%, transparent 70%);\n  filter: blur(10px);\n  animation: bull-breathe 6s ease-in-out infinite;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 0;\n}\n\n@keyframes bull-breathe {\n  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 0.85; }\n  50% { transform: scale(1.12); opacity: 1; }\n}\n\n/* The bull itself — bigger, floating gently */\n.hero-visual img {\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 1;\n  max-width: 165%;\n  max-height: 92vh;\n  height: auto;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 40px rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.15));\n  animation: bull-float 6s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n\n@keyframes bull-float {\n  0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }\n  50% { transform: translateY(-14px); }\n}\n\n/* Soft elliptical shadow that grounds the bull */\n.hero-visual::after {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  bottom: 6%;\n  left: 50%;\n  width: 55%;\n  height: 6%;\n  transform: translateX(-50%);\n  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65), transparent 70%);\n  border-radius: 50%;\n 