ss were served, the page would be styled (the nav would look right — but the screenshot showed UNSTYLED blue links nav). So real CSS isn't loaded.\n\nHmm, wait — look at the screenshot again: nav shows as a vertical list of blue links at top-left, then an inline menu of links, then the ticker, then hero text. That layout = completely unstyled HTML flow. My injected CSS DID style `.hero`, `.container`, `.hero-grid`... but the screenshot was taken BEFORE?? No — I injected, then screenshot showed mostly unstyled. But then the second evaluate shows the mask applied and translateY... So the injection DID take effect (maskLayers:3, transform applied).\n\nWait, actually — the first screenshot: did it capture before injection? Timeline: register was already live; I navigated (reload) → waited; evaluate counted elements (3 dust, 6 embers) → injected styles → returned computed mask info → screenshot. So injection happened before screenshot. But the screenshot shows an unstyled page with the ticker and hero text...\n\nHmm, but actually the ticker rendering requires its own CSS (the TradingView widget embeds its own styles inline — that's why it looks fine). The nav looking like plain blue links means page CSS absent — my injected CSS doesn't cover nav (correct, I only injected hero CSS). But the HERO should look styled: eyebrow/h1/subhead were in the screenshot as plain text (the description shows \"Premium Trading Education\" as separate lines — consistent with the .eyebrow element unstyled, default block display). Hmm — the hero text in the screenshot is cut off mid-paragraph at the bottom. And NO bull visible in the right column.\n\nWait — maybe the screenshot viewport was scrolled to top and the hero is below the fold? No — the description shows the hero text at the bottom edge. The ticker (margin-top:60px) sits between nav and hero. So the hero IS in view, bottom portion visible. The bull should be at the right of the hero... but hero-visual is 36x42px at (195,698) — tiny