be the `.container` in my injection is being overridden by... hmm, actually, is it possible that the REAL css/style.css IS being served now? Let me re-check: the reload might have re-fetched and this environment serves static files from the workspace... Actually earlier preview_logs showed 404 for css/style.css. But maybe after reload with the htmlPath registration attempt... the live preview at 49270 is the OLD server. Hmm.\n\nLet me just check: does the page have any stylesheet loaded? `document.styleSheets.length`, and whether `body` has the font. Let me evaluate more diagnostics: container width, computed grid columns, and whether getComputedStyle(document.body).backgroundColor is #0A0A0A (my injection) — that would confirm my CSS applied.\n\nActually — simpler theory: THE IMG. `max-width: 176%` — percentage max-width against the containing block width. The containing block for a `position: relative` element's percentage is the nearest ancestor block container's CONTENT box... `.hero-visual` is the containing block (position: relative). Its width: the grid cell. If grid cell is normal (640px), img = 1126px. The observed img width 63px ≠ 1126px. So the visual really is 36px wide.\n\nOK here's another thought — maybe `.hero` flex isn't applying and instead `.hero` has default block; `.container` with `width: 100%` but NO box-sizing reset → width:100% + padding 32px*2 = viewport+64 → overflowing, but layout still ~viewport. That doesn't shrink to 72px.\n\nI'm going in circles. Let me get diagnostics: computed widths of .hero, .container, .hero-content, .hero-visual; and check whether my injected style tag exists + whether body bg color applied. Also whether the real stylesheet loaded (styleSheets).\n\nActually — WAIT. I think I've got it. The `.hero-grid` I injected: `display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;` — but is `.hero-grid` also the container? The element has BOTH classes: `class=\"container hero-grid\"`. My `.container` rule sets `width: 100%` — and grid container width = 100% of `.hero`. Fine.\n\nHmm, but what about `align-items: center` on `.hero` and the container being a flex item... flex items have `min-width: auto` — but width:100% overrides.\n\nYou know what, let me just measure. Diagnostics via evaluate.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"The bull image loaded (1536×1024) but the layout collapsed — the hero-visual column is only 36px wide. Something in the flex/grid sizing is off in this unstyled environment. Let me diagnose:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"0pK2A1Jp8gs","toolName":"preview_evaluate","input":{"expression":"(() => {\n  const q = s => { const el = document.querySelector(s); return el ? { cls: el.className, w: Math.round(el.getBoundingClientRect().width), disp: getComputedStyle(el).display } : null; };\n  const sheets = [...document.styleSheets].map(s => s.href || 'inline');\n  return {\n    sheets,\n    bodyBg: getComputedStyle(document.body).backgroundColor,\n    hero: q('.hero'),\n    container: q('.container'),\n    heroGrid: q('.hero-grid'),\n    heroContent: q('.hero-content'),\n    heroVisual: q('.hero-visual'),\n    htmlW: document.documentElement.clientWidth\n  };\n})()"}},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p20-37c49ef6","text":"Now I see it! The viewport is 303px wide (htmlW: 303)! The preview webview is TINY — 303px. So the layout is mobile-sized. My injected CSS has no media query collapsing — the hero-grid stays 2 columns at 303px viewport → each column ~ (262-64)/2 = 99px... but heroVisual is 36px. Hmm, with gap 4rem=64px: (262-64)/2 = 99. heroContent is 99 ✓. heroVisual 36? Odd — the img at max-width:176% would be 63. The visual is flex with the img inside (63px wide, overflowing the 36px cell? The img is 63px wide, but the visual box is 36... the flex container .hero-visual has justify-content:center — the img (63px) overflows the 36px container. Whatever — this is just the tiny preview viewport.\n\nAlso interesting: `sheets` shows `http://127.0.0.1:49270/css/style.css`