 (looking at the screenshot), the text content \"Premium Trading Education / Game Changers\" starts quite far below the nav. If the ticker is thin (like 30px), then between nav-bottom (~65) and text-top there's: ticker (60-95) + hero padding 40 + centering... \n\nThe screenshot shows the text at maybe 30% down the screen. If viewport 900: text top at ~270. Ticker bottom at ~95 (if widget short) or ~110 (if 46px widget). Gap = 160-175px. THAT is \"a bit far\"! And it comes from the hero centering offset: content box 820, grid 855 → overflow 17 top... that gives grid top ~132 not 270. Contradiction again.\n\nUnless the grid height is NOT 855! Maybe max-height: 95vh on the img doesn't size the grid to 855 — maybe the img's height in the visual is limited by the VISUAL's height which is limited by... the hero-content column (470px)? In a grid with 2 columns, the row height = max of the two column contents. If the visual column's img is 95vh (855) tall, the row IS 855. Unless the visual box's height is constrained... `align-items: center` on hero + the flex item... no constraint.\n\nHonestly — measure it. Let me do that now. Then fix.\n\nAlso — one more consideration for the ticker: `margin-top: 60px` — since the nav is ~65px tall and fixed, 60px means the ticker overlaps the nav's lower area slightly or sits just below. The user might want the ticker NOT to have the big 60px gap — but that's needed for nav clearance.\n\nLet me measure the live preview.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"ad","id":"p6-5bcf4520","ad":{"adText":"Add a touch of cozy elegance to your space with this plush blue velvet cushion that instantly elevates any sofa or bed.","title":"Blue Velvet Cushion","cta":"Learn More","url":"https://www.zarahome.com/","favicon":"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.zarahome.com&sz=64","clickUrl":"https://api.trygravity.ai/track/click?p=gAAAAABqc11bj334Xuo-9e-GhMuKyA4pVTWt7U9in58_fur5YqYfSGy2zWT2m0QLBA1r-8qjMYIGqMnPtxEChvFDq57-jKFgJF7QKyMoQ0Apwi