the TradingView widget inside. The hero content should start 8px after the ticker's border. So why a gap?\n\nPossible causes:\n1. **The ticker strip's bottom padding + the hero's padding**: ticker has `padding: 8px 0` — so the ticker's bottom edge includes 8px of padding below the widget, then the border-bottom. Then hero padding-top 8px. Total ≈ 8 + 8 = 16px + the widget's own bottom... The widget itself might have internal padding/margins.\n\n2. **The TradingView widget itself has margins** — the ticker-strip contains `.tradingview-widget-container` — the widget might have its own padding.\n\n3. **The hero content vertical centering**: Wait — with `align-items: flex-start`, the flex item (hero-grid) is top-aligned. But — hmm, is the hero-grid really top-aligned? Let me reconsider: `.hero` is `display: flex; align-items: flex-start` (inline). The `.hero-grid` (`.container.hero-grid`) is the flex item → top-aligned to the content box top. Content box top = hero top + padding-top 8px. So the grid starts 8px below the hero top. The hero top = ticker bottom (no margin between them). So content ≈ 8px below the ticker's border-bottom.\n\nBut WAIT — the hero-grid is a GRID with `align-items: center` (its own property!) — the grid's `align-items: center` affects the grid ITEMS within the grid (the two columns), not the grid container's position. The grid container position = flex-start in the hero. So the grid box top = 8px below ticker. Within the grid, the row height = max(columns) ≈ 676px (bull). The text column content (470px) is vertically CENTERED within the 676px row (align-items: center on the grid). So the TEXT starts at 8 + (676-470)/2 = 8 + 103 = 111px below the ticker! \n\nTHAT's the remaining gap! The grid's `align-items: center` centers the TEXT within the tall row (bull-driven 676px). The hero-content div stretches to 676px (default stretch... wait, `align-items: center` on the grid overrides stretch → the content div is centered vertically, sized to its content 470px). So the text sits ~103px down.\n\nHmm wait — but does the text really center? The grid row is 676 tall. The hero-content column with `align-items: center` → the hero-content div is placed at the vertical center of the row: top = (676-470)/2 = 103. Yes! The text starts ~103px below the grid top.\n\nSo to push the text even higher, I need the text column to be TOP-aligned within the row too. Change the grid's align-items from center to flex-start/stretch — but that's `.hero-grid` global (affects only index.html since other pages use `.container` not `.hero-grid`). `.hero-grid` is only on index.html. \n\nBut wait — the visual (bull) column also centers: `.hero-visual` is `display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center` — the img (676px... wait the img is 176% width = 1014px wide, 676 tall) inside the visual box (576 wide × row height 676). The img is 676 tall = the row height → fills it exactly? The img height 676 = row height 676 (bull-driven). So the img fills the row. Hmm, actually the img is the element that DRIVES the row height (it's the tallest). So img height = row height, no centering issue for the bull.\n\nBut the TEXT (470px) centers within the 676 row → ~103px gap below the ticker. The user sees THIS gap (text starts ~110px down).\n\nFix: make `.hero-grid` align-items top: `align-items: flex-start` on the grid... but then the hero-content div would be at the top of the row (text at 8px below ticker). And the hero-visual div — its img is 676 tall filling the row; with align-items flex-start the visual div is 576 wide × 676 tall, img centered in it (flex center) — fine.\n\nWait — but actually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether the row is really 676 tall on the user's desktop. The img max-width: 176% of the visual column (~576px) = 1014px wide; height = 1014 × 1024/1536 = 676px. Yes, ~676. And `max-height: 95vh` (855) not binding. So row = 676.\n\nThe user's screenshot: the text \"PREMIUM TRADING EDUCATION\" starts... the description say