ck flow from top. So \"Premium Trading Education\" at ~12px below ticker border. Good.\n\nBut also the hero-content's internal structure: eyebrow, h1, p, buttons — they'll flow from the top of the column. Fine.\n\nBut — hmm, wait, one more: the grid `align-items: center` — if I change to flex-start, the hero-visual div (576×676) top-aligned; the img inside is flex-centered (justify-content:center; align-items:center) → img centered in the 676-tall visual → img fills it (676 tall) — no change for the bull. Good.\n\nNow — also reconsider: should I reduce the row height by making the bull smaller? No — user wants the bull big. The text top-alignment is the fix.\n\nWait, actually — hold on. Let me reconsider once more. Is the gap REALLY from grid centering? Let me re-verify with the live preview measurement. Earlier I measured gapTickerToContent: 8px — with my injected CSS which set `.hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }` (stacked!) — in the stacked layout, the grid row height = auto (each column its own row), so the text column was top-anchored → 8px gap. That's why my measurement showed 8px! But on the real desktop (2 columns), the grid row = 676 (bull) and the text centers → ~111px gap. My measurement was misleading because I forced a stacked layout.\n\nSo the user's report makes sense: on their desktop, the text still has a ~100px+ gap from the grid's align-items: center.\n\nFix confirmed:\n1. `.hero-grid`: `align-items: center` → `flex-start`. This is safe — only index.html uses `.hero-grid`.\n2. Hero padding-top: 8px → 12px (a bit of wiggle room; or keep 8 and let the grid top align give the wiggle). The \"wiggle room\" = the padding-top. Let me set 12px.\n3. Optionally reduce the ticker's internal bottom padding (8px)? That's part of the widget's own space — the ticker strip padding 8px 0. I could reduce to `4px 0`? The ticker's border-bottom + padding... The gap between the widget content and the hero = ticker padding-bottom (8) + border + hero p