nt to Ethical Practices\n- User Responsibility\n- Transparency of Services\n- No Guarantee of Results\n\nStructure: `<details class=\"disclaimer\">` with `<summary>Terms & Conditions</summary>` and inside, either paragraphs or sub-headings. The current disclaimer has just a `<p>`. For T&C, I can use a few `<p>` blocks with `<strong>` lead-ins (e.g., \"<strong>Business Transparency & Compliance Statement.</strong> ...\"). That keeps it classy and readable without heavy styling.\n\nContent draft:\n```\n<strong>Business Transparency &amp; Compliance Statement.</strong> Reality FX operates with full transparency as a financial education and mentorship provider. We clearly disclose the nature of our services, the pricing of every program, and our regulatory position as an educational platform — not a licensed investment advisory firm. We comply with applicable consumer-protection principles and are always open to questions about how we operate.\n<strong>Commitment to Ethical Practices.</strong> We are committed to honest marketing, fair pricing, and respectful conduct in every interaction. We do not make false promises, misrepresent results, or pressure anyone into a purchase. Every claim we make about our programs reflects genuine student and client experience.\n<strong>User Responsibility.</strong> Trading involves substantial risk. You are responsible for the decisions you make with your own capital, for applying what you learn, and for seeking independent financial advice where appropriate. Our courses and mentorship are educational tools — your results depend on your effort, discipline, and market conditions.\n<strong>Transparency of Services.</strong> Each program clearly states what is included: lessons, mentorship, signals, account management, and support. What is not included is equally clearly stated. If anything is ever unclear, we invite you to ask before you enrol.\n<strong>No Guarantee of Results.</strong> We do not and cannot guarantee profits. No mentor, 