fund Policy</summary>\n            <h4>The Honest Guarantee</h4>\n            <p>We are not here to take your money and disappear. If you complete the first chapter of any course and\n              genuinely feel it is not for you, email us within 7 days of purchase and we will refund you in full — no\n              questions, no friction, no hard feelings. We would rather earn a client for life than keep a fee from\n              someone who felt misled.</p>\n            <h4>Why Chapter One Is Deliberately Light</h4>\n            <p>Chapter 1 is your orientation — a gentle introduction that lays the groundwork in plain language. The\n              real depth arrives in Chapter 2 and beyond: the precise entry models, risk mathematics, live session\n              breakdowns, and the discipline frameworks that take time to build properly. We tell you this upfront so\n              the first chapter never feels like a bait-and-switch.</p>\n            <h4>See the Depth Before You Commit</h4>\n            <p>Because we never want you buying on faith, the full curriculum outline — every chapter, module, and\n              lesson — is available to you before purchase. Review what Chapters 2 to 13 actually contain and judge the\n              level of detail for yourself before spending a cent. Contact us for a guided preview of any later chapter\n              before you buy; we are happy to show you the depth.</p>\n            <h4>After Chapter One</h4>\n            <p>Once you have completed the first chapter and continued into the full program, refunds no longer apply —\n              by then you have seen the depth, the value, and the standard of teaching, and full curriculum access has\n              been delivered. If you are ever unhappy with your experience, contact us anyway: we resolve issues fairly,\n              case by case, because a single unhappy student is a cost we never want to carry.</p>\n          </details>\n```\n\nThis addresses the user's logic co