rap: wrap; gap: 1rem`. So copyright p on the left, dropdowns group on the right. With `align-items: center` on footer-bottom, the flex children (p + legal-dropdowns) center vertically — fine.\n\n   Potential issue: when multiple details are open, the dropdowns expand and could get very tall, pushing the layout. Not a bug per se.\n\n   Issue: `.legal-dropdowns` uses `justify-content: flex-end` — on narrow screens before 640px, the wrap could squeeze. Fine.\n\n2. `.disclaimer` — added `overflow: hidden` and `position: relative`. The `::before` is a 3px left accent with `scaleY(0.3)` → `scaleY(1)` on hover/open. With `border-radius: 8px`, the `::before` at top-left could poke out of the rounded corner — but `overflow: hidden` clips it. However, there's a subtle problem: `overflow: hidden` on a `<details>` element can interfere with... actually, a bigger concern: when a `details` is open and its content overflows, `overflow: hidden` clips nothing harmful since details grows. OK.\n\n   Wait — an important issue: `overflow: hidden` on the `<details>` combined with `summary::after { margin-left: auto }` — no conflict.\n\n   Another subtle issue: `.disclaimer::before` has `height: 100%` and `border-radius: 8px 0 0 8px` wasn't set — the accent bar is a straight 3px vertical bar; with `overflow: hidden` it gets clipped at the rounded corner — that's the intent, fine.\n\n   Actually, a real edge: `overflow: hidden` on `<details>` clips focus outlines and can clip the `summary::after` chevron? No.\n\n   One genuine concern: **`transform` on `::before` with `scaleY` and `transition`** — fine.\n\n3. `summary { display: flex; list-style: none; }` — `list-style: none` is needed for Firefox's default marker; `::-webkit-details-marker { display: none }` handles Chrome/Safari. This is the correct cross-browser approach. Good.\n\n   Edge: Firefox `list-style: none` on summary works. Good.\n\n4. `summary::after` — `margin-left: auto` pushes the `+` to the right. Good. `padding-left: 1rem` gives spacing. Fine.\n\n5. `.disclaimer h4` — uses `--font-heading` (Playfair), gold color, margins. Global h4 rules? The site likely has generic h4 styling; this specificity `.disclaimer h4` (0,1,1) beats `h4` (0,0,1). Fine.\n\n6. Media query `@media (max-width: 640px)` centers `.legal-dropdowns`. The footer-bottom column breakpoint is at 640px (line 1726). Consistent. Good.\n\n7. One issue: the `.disclaimer:hover` box-shadow `0 0 24px rgba(201,162,39,.07)` — subtle, fine.\n\n8. **Potential real issue**: `overflow: hidden` on `.disclaimer` clips the hover `box-shadow`? No — box-shadow is painted outside the element but `overflow` doesn't clip box-shadows (box-shadow is not clipped by overflow on the element itself; it's clipped only by ancestors with overflow + the element's own border... actually no: an element's own `overflow: hidden` does NOT clip its own box-shadow). Fine.\n\n9. The `transition` includes `box-shadow`, `border-color`, `background` — smooth. Good.\n\n10. A subtle a11y/UX point: `details` open/close isn't animated (content pops). Not required.\n\n11. **Actual potential bug**: In `.disclaimer summary::after`, `content: '+'` — but on the contact.html in-content disclaimer (`Risk Disclaimer & Legal Notice`), the summary text is long; the chevron will be pushed right with `margin-left: auto` — fine.\n\n12. Another consideration: `.legal-dropdowns .disclaimer { max-width: 100% }` — fine.\n\n13. `h4:first-child` margin-top: 1rem — since h4s come after summary, the first h4's margin-top gives separation from summary. Good.\n\n**HTML changes:**\n\n- 8 pages wrapped the footer disclaimer in `.legal-dropdowns` and added Terms & Refund. The verified code search shows each page has exactly 3 summaries (Risk Disclaimer, Terms & Conditions, Refund Policy) plus contact's in-content one at line 208 untouched. Balanced.\n\n- Potential issues to flag:\n  1. **No `<a>` / no way to open these programmatically** — not needed.\n  2. **Content duplication across 8 pages** — the same large T&C and Refund blocks are copy-pasted into every HTML file. If they ever edit the policy, they must edit 8 files. This is a maintenance concern but consistent with the site's static multi-page approach (the risk disclaimer was already duplicated). Could suggest consolidating later, but the site is static with no templating, so acceptable — though worth mentioning as an improvement (e.g., extract to a shared snippet or include via JS).\n  3. **The user's core ask — \"no guarantee of results\" etc.** — all 5 requested T&C items present. Refund policy abundance mindset present, chapter-1 logic addressed. Good.\n  4. **Legal caveat**: The refund policy says \"email us within 7 days of purchase\" — the user's actual requirement was \"refund after chapter one if not happy\". The copy says \"If you complete the first chapter ... within 7 days of purchase\" — combines both. Reasonable. But one thing: the user said \"after that refunds don't apply\" — copy covers it. Fine.\n  5. **`h4` styling conflict**: check if the site has a global `h4` rule that sets `text-transform` or similar — minor.\n  6. One more: `summary::after` uses `+` character and rotates to `×` (45°) when open — good.\n  7. **Possible issue**: `.disclaimer` `padding: 1.5rem` with `overflow: hidden` — the gold `::before` accent at left:0 with the rounded corner 8px — the bar's top corner is clipped; visually the bar starts flush at the top edge. Fine.\n\n  8. **Edge case worth flagging**: `details[open]` retains hover state when open; `[open]::before` stays at opacity 1 — intended.\n\n  9. **Real potential problem**: In the footer, `.footer-bottom` has `align-items: center`. With `.legal-dropdowns { align-items: flex-start }`, dropdown cards top-align relative to each other. Fine.\n\n  10. **Potential bug**: `overflow: hidden` on details — in Firefox, `details` with `overflow: hidden` clips the bottom padding? No.\n\n  11. One thing I want to double-check: the `.disclaimer p { margin-top: 1rem }` — the first `<p>` after an `<h4>` will have margin-top: 1rem, plus h4 margin-bottom 0.35rem — spacing ok.\n\n  12. **Suggest improvement**: an animation for the open/close would be classier, but details can't animate height easily. Not needed.\n\n  13. **Accessibility**: `summary` is keyboard accessible by default. Good.\n\n  14. A genuinely useful critique: **the same legal blocks are duplicated 8×** — if the user wants to tweak the refund wording later (very likely given they iterated a lot), they'd need to edit 8 files. Could propose extracting into a shared JS-injected block or a server-side include later. Also the formspree AJAX handler targets `form[action*=\"formspree.io\"]` — irrelevant here.\n\n  15. Also possible concern: **`<h4>` inside `<details>`** — semantics fine.\n\n  16. Another: `.disclaimer:hover` applies to the in-content contact disclaimer too — consistent styling, good.\n\n  17. Wait — one real issue: **`summary::after` `margin-left: auto`** — in flex, `summary` is `display: flex`, the text node is a flex item (anonymous), then `::after` with `margin-left: auto` pushes to the right edge. Works.\n\n  18. **Firefox default marker**: `list-style: none` removes it in Firefox. Good.\n\n  19. Potential styling bug: `.disclaimer` had `margin-top: 2rem` originally (for in-content usage like contact line 207 and evaluation). The `.legal-dropdowns .disclaimer { margin-top: 0 }` overrides within the footer. Good.\n\n  20. **One more check — `.disclaimer[open]::before` opacity 1** — when a dropdown is open and NOT hovered, the left accent shows — nice persistent indicator.\n\nOverall the changes look solid. The main critical feedback:\n\n1. **8× content duplication** — maintenance risk; suggest a shared snippet/partial or JS injection so future edits are one-place. (Biggest practical critique given the user iterates a lot.)\n2. **Minor**: consider `scroll-margin`/no — not relevant.\n3. **Minor**: `overflow: hidden` may clip the focus ring on the summary when tabbing (keyboard a11y) — the focus outline on the summary inside a rounded element with overflow:hidden would be clipped at the 8px radius. Could add `outline-offset: 2px` or `outline: none + custom` focus style for consistency with the site's theme. The site likely has custom focus styles already.\n4. **Minor**: The chevron `+` character at `font-size: 1.05rem` with `line-height: 1` — could misalign vertically; negligible.\n5. Could suggest making the refund/terms dropdowns also consistent in the mobile menu — not needed.\n\nAlso double-check the requirements from the review prompt:\n- `::before` with overflow:hidden on rounded corners — OK (intended clip).\n- h4 clash with global h4 — `.disclaimer h4` specificity wins; but if there's a global `h4 { margin: ... }` it might add extra margins — the `.disclaimer h4` sets margins explicitly, overriding. OK.\n- `summary::after` margin-left auto — works.\n- Firefox vs webkit marker — handled via `list-style: none` + `::-webkit-details-marker`. OK.\n- `.legal-dropdowns` flex-end with footer-bottom wrap — on wide screens, p left, dropdowns right; if wrapped to next line, justify-end keeps them right — the mobile media query centers at 640px. Slight gap: between 640px and ~768px, dropdowns may wrap below the copyright right-aligned, looking slightly odd, but acceptable. Actually with `flex-wrap: wrap` on footer-bottom and gap 1rem, at mid widths the legal-dropdowns could sit on its own row right-aligned — fine visually.\n- HTML duplication/malformed blocks — verified balanced (3 summaries each, 8 legal-dropdowns).\n- contact in-content disclaimer untouched — yes, still line 208, benefits from hover styles. Good.\n\nOne more genuine issue to flag: **the `.disclaimer` hover glow `box-shadow` on the footer dropdowns which contain lots of text** — fine.\n\nAnother: **`summary` `letter-spacing: 0.1em` → 0.12em on hover** — text shifts slightly (letters spread) which can cause a tiny layout jump, but it's a common effect; minor.\n\nAlso: `content: '+'` on `::after` — on some systems the `+` glyph vs `×` at 45° rotation — fine.\n\nI think the review should be brief with the duplication maintenance concern as the top item, plus small notes on focus-visible clipping and possibly a smooth open animation (optional). Also validate that refund policy solves the user's chapter-1 logic — it does via \"curriculum outline available before purchase\" + guided preview. Good.\n\nKeep it concise per instructions.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"<think>Let me review the changes against the codebase context I have:\n\n**CSS (style.css):**\n- `.disclaimer` now has `overflow: hidden` + `position: relative`; `::before` is a 3px gold left accent with `scaleY(0.3)→1` reveal. `overflow: hidden` clips it to the 8px radius — intended, works.\n- `summary` uses `list-style: none` (Firefox) + `::-webkit-details-marker { display: none }` (Chrome/Safari) — correct cross-browser marker removal.\n- `summary::after` `+` chevron with `margin-left: auto` in a flex summary pushes right, rotates 45° when `[open]`. Good.\n- `.disclaimer h4` (0,1,1) beats any global `h4` (0,0,1). Sets margins explicitly. No clash.\n- `.legal-dropdowns` flex, justify-end; media query at 640px matches the footer-bottom column breakpoint (line 1726). Consistent.\n- One subtle thing: `overflow: hidden` on the details will clip the keyboard focus outline at the rounded corner (a11y). Worth a custom focus-visible style.\n\n**HTML (8 pages):**\n- Verified: 3 summaries each, 8 `.legal-dropdowns` containers, contact.html's in-content \"Risk Disclaimer & Legal Notice\" (line 208) untouched and inherits the styling. Balanced tags.\n- All 5 requested T&C items present; refund policy covers abundance mindset, 7-day/Chapter-1 window, and the chapter-1 \"looks thin\" problem is addressed with the pre-purchase curriculum outline + guided preview.\n\n**Main critique:** the same ~40-line T&C and Refund blocks are now copy-pasted into 8 files. Any wording tweak (and this user iterates a lot — they'll likely tweak refund language) means editing 8 files. Since the site is static with no templating, this matches the existing pattern (risk disclaimer was already duplicated), but it's the biggest practical maintenance risk. Could be injected once from a shared JS file or a small include later.</｜｜DSML｜｜parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜invoke>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜tool_calls>"}]},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p23-c551de95","text":"The reviewer approved the changes with two useful notes:\n1. Content is duplicated across 8 pages (maintenance risk) — acceptable for static site, matches existing pattern. Could offer a JS-injection approach.\n2. Focus outline on summary could be clipped by overflow:hidden — worth adding a focus-visible style for accessibility.\n\nLet me add a small focus-visible style for the summary (classy gold focus ring), which aligns with the site's theme. Quick edit:\n\n```css\n.disclaimer summary:focus-visible {\n  outline: 1px solid rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.5);\n  outline-offset: 3px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n```\n\nThen mark todos complete and write the final summary. This is a tiny CSS addition — no need for a full re-review.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"The reviewer approved everything and flagged one worth fixing: keyboard focus could get clipped by the rounded corners. Adding a classy gold focus ring:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"0yeYf9pK4wo","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css","replacements":[{"oldString":".disclaimer summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n  display: none;\n}","newString":".disclaimer summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n  display: none;\n}\n\n.disclaimer summary:focus-visible {\n  outline: 1px solid rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.55);\n  outline-offset: 3px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}","allowMultiple":false}]}},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"},{"kind":"tool","id":"0yfxp3MqvnI","toolName":"write_todos","input":{"todos":[{"task":"Upgrade .disclaimer CSS: golden hover, gold left accent, custom rotating chevron, open-state styling + .legal-dropdowns container","completed":true},{"task":"Add Terms & Conditions dropdown to footer of all 8 pages (Transparency, Ethics, User Responsibility, No Guarantee)","completed":true},{"task":"Add Refund Policy dropdown to footer of all 8 pages (abundance mindset + chapter-1 depth solution)","completed":true},{"task":"Verify in live preview: hover states, open/close chevron, layout","completed":true},{"task":"Code review pass","completed":true}]}},{"kind":"text","text":"Done! Every page's footer now has **three** dropdowns — Risk Disclaimer, **Terms & Conditions**, and **Refund Policy** — all with the classy golden treatment.\n\n## ✨ The styling (matches the site's gold language)\n- **Hover:** the card's border warms to gold, a soft gold glow rises behind it, and the summary text brightens to `--accent-gold-light` with a subtle letter-spread\n- **Gold left accent bar** — a thin vertical gold gradient line slides down the left edge on hover, and *stays* lit while the dropdown is open, so open items are visible at a glance\n- **Custom chevron** — the native marker is gone, replaced by a gold `+` that smoothly rotates 45° into an `×` when open\n- Gold serif sub-headings inside the content, keyboard focus ring in gold, and a mobile rule that centers the trio on small screens (matching the stacked footer)\n\n## 📜 Terms & Conditions\nAll five sections you asked for, written in the site's voice: **Business Transparency & Compliance Statement**, **Commitment to Ethical Practices**, **Transparency of Services**, **User Responsibility**, and **No Guarantee of Results** — with a hard stance on profit guarantees: *\"Anyone who guarantees trading income is not being honest with you; we will never be that person.\"*\n\n## 💛 Refund Policy — the logic problem, solved\nThe abundance-mindset guarantee is in: *\"We are not here to take your money and disappear\"* — full refund, no questions, if you complete Chapter 1 and aren't convinced. But your concern (Chapter 1 looks thin → false refunds) gets three built-in answers:\n\n1. **Explicit framing** — the policy states upfront that Chapter 1 is a deliberately light orientation and the depth lands in Chapter 2+, so nobody feels bait-and-switched\n2. **See the depth before you buy** — the full curriculum outline (Chapters 2–13) is available pre-purchase, plus a **guided preview of any later chapter on request** — so buyers verify substance *before* spending, which is what actually stops refunds\n3. **A clean boundary** — refunds apply only within the 7-day/Chapter-1 window; after that, full access has been delivered. It also leaves a goodwill clause (\"resolve issues fairly, case by case\") so it reads generous, not rigid\n\nVerified across all 8 pages (3 dropdowns each, contact's in-content disclaimer untouched), plus a code-review pass that added the keyboard focus ring. Reload any page and hover the footer dropdowns — they feel right at home.\n\nIf you'd like, I can also make the pre-purchase curriculum preview a real feature (a \"peek at Chapter 2\" button on the Programs page) so the policy's promise is backed by an actual page."},{"kind":"tool","id":"0yhJxX8zFxw","toolName":"suggest_prompts","input":{"prompts":[{"prompt":"Add a real 'peek inside Chapter 2' feature on the Programs page (e.g. a sample lesson breakdown or video) so the Refund Policy's 'see the depth before you commit' promise is backed by an actual page.","label":"Build the Chapter 2 preview page"},{"prompt":"The Terms & Conditions and Refund Policy blocks are now duplicated across 8 HTML files. Move them into a single shared source (e.g. injected via main.js) so future wording edits only need one change.","label":"Extract legal text into one shared file"},{"prompt":"Add visible 'Terms & Conditions' and 'Refund Policy' links (that open the footer dropdowns) alongside the copyright line for better discoverability.","label":"Add legal links to the footer nav"}]}},{"kind":"changes","id":"p24-c551de95","files":[{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\careers.html","status":"modified","lockfile":false,"binary":false,"adds":54,"dels":6,"patch":"Index: REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\careers.html\n===================================================================\n--- REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\careers.html\tbefore\n+++ REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\careers.html\tafter\n@@ -808,12 +808,60 @@\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"footer-bottom\">\n         <p>&copy; 2026 Reality FX. All rights reserved.</p>\n-        <details class=\"disclaimer\">\n-          <summary>Risk Disclaimer</summary>\n-          <p>Trading foreign exchange, commodities, and other financial instruments carries a high level of risk and may\n-            not be suitable for all investors. Past performance is not indicative of future results. Reality FX provides\n-            educational content and mentorship only. We do not guarantee profits.</p>\n-        </details>\n+        <div class=\"legal-dropdowns\">\n+          <details class=\"disclaimer\">\n+            <summary>Risk Disclaimer</summary>\n+            <p>Trading foreign exchange, commodities, and other financial instruments carries a high level of risk and may\n+              not be suitable for all investors. Past performance is not indicative of future results. Reality FX provides\n+              educational content and mentorship only. We do not guarantee profits.</p>\n+          </details>\n+          <details class=\"disclaimer\">\n+            <summary>Terms &amp; Conditions</summary>\n+            <h4>Business Transparency &amp; Compliance Statement</h4>\n+            <p>Reality FX operates as a transparent education and mentorship provider. We are committed to honesty in\n+              how we market, price, and deliver our services. Every program detail — what is included, what is not, and\n+              what you can reasonably expect — is stated clearly before you purchase.</p>\n+            <h4>Commitment to Ethical Practices</h4>\n+            <p>We hold ourselves to the highest ethical standards. We never guarantee profits, never pressure you into\n+              decisions, and never sell you something that is not in your interest. Our mentorship is educational\n+              guidance, not financial advice — and we will always tell you the difference.</p>\n+            <h4>Transparency of Services</h4>\n+            <p>You will always know exactly what you are paying for: the curriculum, the mentorship hours, the duration\n+              of access, and any additional resources. If a program changes, we will tell you before you commit — never\n+              after.</p>\n+            <h4>User Responsibility</h4>\n+            <p>You are responsible for the decisions you make with your own capital. We provide the education, tools,\n+              and discipline framework; applying them consistently is your part of the partnership. Trading involves\n+              risk, and no educational program can remove that risk — it can only prepare you to manage it.</p>\n+            <h4>No Guarantee of Results</h4>\n+            <p>Results depend on your effort, consistency, capital, and the markets themselves. Past performance — ours\n+              or any trader's — is not a promise of future results. Anyone who guarantees trading income is not being\n+              honest with you; we will never be that person.</p>\n+          </details>\n+          <details class=\"disclaimer\">\n+            <summary>Refund Policy</summary>\n+            <h4>The Honest Guarantee</h4>\n+            <p>We are not here to take your money and disappear. If you complete the first chapter of any course and\n+              genuinely feel it is not for you, email us within 7 days of purchase and we will refund you in full — no\n+              questions, no friction, no hard feelings. We would rather earn a client for life than keep a fee from\n+              someone who felt misled.</p>\n+            <h4>Why Chapter One Is Deliberately Light</h4>\n+            <p>Chapter 1 is your orientation — a gentle introduction that lays the groundwork in plain language. The\n+              real depth arrives in Chapter 2 and beyond: the precise entry models, risk mathematics, live session\n+              breakdowns, and the discipline frameworks that take time to build properly. We tell you this upfront so\n+              the first chapter never feels like a bait-and-switch.</p>\n+            <h4>See the Depth Before You Commit</h4>\n+            <p>Because we never want you buying on faith, the full curriculum outline — every chapter, module, and\n+              lesson — is available to you before purchase. Review what Chapters 2 to 13 actually contain and judge the\n+              level of detail for yourself before spending a cent. Contact us for a guided preview of any later chapter\n+              before you buy; we are happy to show you the depth.</p>\n+            <h4>After Chapter One</h4>\n+            <p>Once you have completed the first chapter and continued into the full program, refunds no longer apply —\n+              by then you have seen the depth, the value, and the standard of teaching, and full curriculum access has\n+              been delivered. If you are ever unhappy with your experience, contact us anyway: we resolve issues fairly,\n+              case by case, because a single unhappy student is a cost we never want to carry.</p>\n+          </details>\n+        </div>\n       </div>\n     </div>\n   </footer>\n","tooLarge":false},{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\contact.html","status":"modified","lockfile":false,"binary":false,"adds":54,"dels":6,"patch":"Index: REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\contact.html\n===================================================================\n--- REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\contact.html\tbefore\n+++ REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\contact.html\tafter\n@@ -283,12 +283,60 @@\n       </div>\r\n