 the hero to look like the reference — the key new elements visible in the reference:\n1. **A large dust explosion/cloud at the base** where the legs are — a big, layered, realistic dust cloud spread at the bottom\n2. **Golden circular arc lines** framing the upper right (like speed arcs / circular orbit lines behind the bull)\n3. **More fine dust particles scattered** around\n\nLet me look at what the reference image shows more carefully:\n- The bull is a metallic gold/black charging bull\n- There's a big cloud of dust/debris at the bottom (golden-tinted dust)\n- Circular arc lines around the upper right of the bull (thin golden rings/circles)\n- Fine golden particles floating\n- Speed lines\n\nSo the user wants:\n1. More dust scattered around (a bigger, denser dust cloud at the base — like an explosion)\n2. Golden circular arc lines framing the upper right (like orbital rings)\n3. Fine particles\n\nSince I can't see the images directly (they're described by a vision model), the key takeaway from the descriptions: The reference shows a bull with \"Fine golden particle effects and circular abstract arc lines frame the upper right\" and dust \"kicking up dust and debris from the ground.\"\n\nSo the plan:\n1. **Add golden orbital/arc rings** to the upper right of the bull — thin circular arcs (SVG or CSS border circles with gradient strokes) that frame the bull\n2. **Enhance the dust at the base** — add a bigger, denser dust explosion at the bottom where the legs are — layered dust clouds with particles that spread outward\n3. **More dust particles** — small blurred dots scattered around the ground area\n\nLet me design this carefully with CSS:\n\n**Element 1: Golden arc rings (upper right)**\n- Use 2-3 concentric circles (border rings) positioned top-right, partially visible, with gold gradient borders and soft glow\n- Could be SVG circles with stroke-dasharray for partial arcs — elegant\n- Position: right side, upper area, behind the bull\n\n**Element 2: Base dust explosion**\n- A large layered dust cloud at the bottom center/right where the legs would be\n- Multiple radial-gradient blobs, blurred, in gold/brown tones, animating (billow outward and upward)\n- Plus small particles (dust specks) that float outward\n\n**Element 3: More scattered particles**\n- Small gold/bronze blurred dots scattered around the base and sides\n\nLet me write this. I'll add to the HTML (in the hero-visual div) and the CSS.\n\nLet me look at the existing hero-visual markup again:\n```html\n<div class=\"hero-visual\">\n  <img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,...\" alt=\"Reality FX Bull Logo\">\n  <div class=\"sweep\"></div>\n  <div class=\"sweep-2\"></div>\n  <span class=\"spark\" ...>x5</span>\n  <!-- Golden dust storm -->\n  <div class=\"dust-cloud\" style=\"width:55%;height:42%;left:46%;top:56%;\"></div>\n  <div class=\"dust-cloud\" style=\"width:42%;height:34%;left:64%;top:30%;animation-delay:3.6s;\"></div>\n  <div class=\"dust-cloud\" style=\"width:38%;height:30%;left:58%;top:72%;animation-delay:7.2s;\"></div>\n  <!-- Dust particles -->\n  <span class=\"ember\" ...>x6</span>\n</div>\n```\n\nThe dust-cloud currently: radial gradient gold, blur 10px, mix-blend screen, animating billow. The user wants \"dust scattered around and all the effects\" like the reference image.\n\nThe reference image description (Image 1): \"Fine golden particle effects and circular abstract arc lines frame the upper right.\" and \"a dynamic, detailed digital illustration of a powerful charging bull made of black and gleaming metallic gold, kicking up dust and debris from the ground.\"\n\nImage 2: \"An artistic graphic of an aggressive charging bull rendered in glowing gold/bronze metallic lines and highlights against the dark background, kicking up dust at the bottom.\"\n\nSo the key additions:\n1. **Circular abstract arc lines** in the upper right — golden orbital arcs\n2. **Dust kicking up at the bottom** — bigger, more realistic dust cloud at the base\n\nThe current site already has dust-clouds but they're positioned around the middle-right (46-64% left, 30-72% top). The reference shows the dust at the BOTTOM (where legs would be), spreading outward and upward.\n\nSo my changes:\n1. Add **golden arc rings** (upper right) — I'll add SVG arcs or CSS rings. SVG with stroke-dasharray gives partial circles elegantly. Add 2-3 arcs with different radii, rotating slowly.\n2. Add **base dust explosion** — a bigger dust layer at the bottom (0-30% from bottom), with particles spreading outward and upward.\n3. Add **more dust particles** (small blurred dots) scattered around the base.\n\nLet me implement:\n\n**HTML additions inside .hero-visual:**\n```html\n<!-- Golden orbital arcs framing the upper right -->\n<svg class=\"hero-arcs\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 400\" fill=\"none\">\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-1\" cx=\"260\" cy=\"150\" r=\"120\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"240 520\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-2\" cx=\"260\" cy=\"150\" r=\"170\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"120 950\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-3\" cx=\"260\" cy=\"150\" r=\"80\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"90 410\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.45\"/>\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"arcGold\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#E5C158\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#C9A227\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Ground dust explosion — where the legs dissolve -->\n<div class=\"dust-burst\"></div>\n<div class=\"dust-burst dust-burst-2\"></div>\n<div class=\"dust-burst dust-burst-3\"></div>\n\n<!-- Scattered dust specks -->\n<span class=\"dust-speck\" style=\"left:30%;top:78%;...\"></span>\n... etc\n```\n\n**CSS:**\n```css\n/* Golden orbital arcs */\n.hero-arcs {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 90%;\n  height: 90%;\n  right: -8%;\n  top: -4%;\n  z-index: 0;\n  opacity: 0.8;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n.hero-arcs .arc {\n  transform-origin: center;\n  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgba(201,162,39,0.35));\n}\n.arc-1 { animation: arc-spin 26s linear infinite; }\n.arc-2 { animation: arc-spin 40s linear infinite reverse; }\n.arc-3 { animation: arc-spin 18s linear infinite; }\n@keyframes arc-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }\n\n/* Ground dust burst */\n.dust-burst {\n  position: absolute;\n  bottom: 2%;\n  left: 30%;\n  width: 70%;\n  height: 40%;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background:\n    radial-gradient(ellipse at 40% 80%, rgba(201,162,39,0.28), transparent 60%),\n    radial-gradient(ellipse at 65% 90%, rgba(201,162,39,0.18), transparent 55%);\n  filter: blur(14px);\n  mix-blend-mode: screen;\n  opacity: 0.55;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 0;\n  animation: dust-burst-pulse 6s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n```\n\nHmm wait — the bull is positioned with the mask so that the bottom melts into the page. The dust burst at the base should look like the dust explosion in the reference. Let me think about positioning. The hero-visual img is `transform: translateY(5vh)` and max-height 95vh — huge. The dust-clouds are around 46-64% left. The bull is charging to the left (or right?). The reference image shows the bull charging forward — with the head lowered. Dust kicks up from behind/below.\n\nActually the exact look: \"kicking up dust and debris from the ground\" — dust cloud at ground level, below the bull. Also the reference shows the bottom section is a big dust cloud.\n\nGiven the current bull has mask so bottom melts away, adding a big dust cloud at the bottom will blend the bull into the dust naturally — exactly what the user asked for earlier (\"On the bulls feet/legs, the mud/dust... make it look smoother or blended\").\n\nSo the plan:\n1. **Golden arc rings top-right** — SVG with animated rotation + drop-shadow glow\n2. **Ground dust explosion** — bigger, layered dust at the bottom, animated