s linear infinite; }\n\n@keyframes arc-orbit {\n  from { transform: rotate(0deg); }\n  to { transform: rotate(360deg); }\n}\n```\n\nWait — for SVG circles, rotating around the center: the circles are centered at cx=260, cy=150. If I set transform-origin to that point in CSS, the circle rotates around its own center, which looks like spinning arcs. That works — the arcs will sweep around, like orbital rings. \n\nActually, a cleaner approach for \"arc lines\": rotating a partial circle around its center gives a spinning ring feel. That's a nice classy effect. Alternatively, keep them static with a gentle opacity shimmer. Slow rotation (20-46s) is elegant and subtle.\n\nHmm, but actually the reference image shows static arc lines (circular abstract arcs framing the upper right) — like speed arcs or trajectory curves. Slow rotation gives life though. Let me do very slow rotation — feels alive without being distracting. I'll go with slow orbit + a subtle glow pulse.\n\nFor the dust burst at the base:\n\n```css\n/* ── Ground dust explosion — the bull charges out of a cloud ── */\n.dust-burst {\n  position: absolute;\n  bottom: -2%;\n  left: 26%;\n  width: 72%;\n  height: 42%;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background:\n    radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 55% at 35% 85%, rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.22), transparent 70%),\n    radial-gradient(ellipse 45% 45% at 60% 92%, rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.16), transparent 65%),\n    radial-gradient(ellipse 40% 40% at 80% 88%, rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.12), transparent 60%);\n  filter: blur(12px);\n  mix-blend-mode: screen;\n  opacity: 0.5;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 0;\n  animation: dust-burst-breathe 7s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n\n.dust-burst-2 {\n  width: 50%;\n  height: 32%;\n  left: 8%;\n  bottom: 6%;\n  animation-delay: 2.3s;\n  opacity: 0.38;\n}\n\n.dust-burst-3 {\n  width: 36%;\n  height: 26%;\n  left: 55%;\n  bottom: 16%;\n  animation-delay: 4.6s;\n  opacity: 0.3;\n}\n\n@keyframes dust-burst-breathe {\n  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1) translateY(0); opacity: 0.45; }\n  50% { transform: scale(1.08) translateY(-6px); opacity: 0.7; }\n}\n```\n\nFor specks:\n\n```css\n/* ── Fine dust specks scattered around the base ── */\n.dust-speck {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 3px;\n  height: 3px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background: rgba(229, 193, 88, 0.8);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 8px 1px rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.35);\n  filter: blur(0.5px);\n  opacity: 0;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 1;\n  animation: speck-drift 9s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n\n@keyframes speck-drift {\n  0% { transform: translate(0, 0); opacity: 0; }\n  15% { opacity: 0.7; }\n  60% { transform: translate(-18px, -26px); opacity: 0.3; }\n  100% { transform: translate(-34px, -52px); opacity: 0; }\n}\n```\n\nSpeck positions: scattered at the bottom around the bull — left 20-80%, top 60-90%.\n\nNow, HTML — add after the existing elements:\n\n```html\n<!-- Golden orbital arcs framing the upper right -->\n<svg class=\"hero-arcs\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 400\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"arcGold\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#F0D97A\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#C9A227\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-1\" cx=\"255\" cy=\"150\" r=\"130\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"255 560\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-2\" cx=\"255\" cy=\"150\" r=\"180\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"120 1010\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.55\"/>\n  <circle class=\"arc arc-3\" cx=\"255\" cy=\"150\" r=\"85\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"100 435\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.4\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Ground dust explosion — the bull charges out of a cloud -->\n<div class=\"dust-burst\"></div>\n<div class=\"dust-burst dust-burst-2\"></div>\n<div class=\"dust-burst dust-burst-3\"></div>\n\n<!-- Fine dust specks scatter