sign question: the mask on `.hero-visual` makes the whole thing blend. The arcs fading at the edges could actually be fine/desirable (soft blend). But the reviewer is right that they may be too faded. However, since I can't easily verify in the sandbox (no stylesheet loads), I should keep the mask behavior consistent with the existing design — the bull itself is masked the same way, so arcs fading at edges is consistent. I'll leave the mask as is but bump arc opacity a bit so they read clearly.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The mask on .hero-visual applies to all children. The arcs at top:-14% right:-16% — position is relative to the container. The mask ellipse is at 52% 55% with black 48% and transparent 86%. So points at distance ratio >86% of the ellipse are transparent. The arcs are at the top-right corner — near 90-100% of the ellipse extent — so they'd be heavily faded there. But the arcs orbit, and parts of the orbit will pass through the visible zone. It's a soft, ambient effect — acceptable, and actually helps them \"blend\" like the reference shows arcs framing around the bull against the dark bg.\n\nActually, thinking about it more: in the reference image, the arc lines are visible in the upper right. If the mask fades them too much, they'll be nearly invisible. A safer approach: the mask on the container was designed for the bull image's edge blending. The arcs and dust are decorative additions — I could raise their base opacity and make sure they're visible. Since the mask will fade the outermost 14%, the arcs centered in the upper-right region will still be partially visible.\n\nLet me be pragmatic: \n- Rename id to arcGoldHero\n- Fix the hover animation-duration to single values\n- Give the dust a persistent floor opacity (0.15 min at rest) so it's always \"scattered around\"\n- Bump arc opacities slightly (0.6/0.35/0.45 are fine as they are — the drop-shadow adds visibility)\n- Add a mobile tweak: reduce arcs/dust size at ≤968px so they don't dominate the shrunken bull\n\nLet me make these edits.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"The reviewer confirmed the implementation is solid and flagged 4 refinements. Let me apply the valuable ones — unique gradient id, fixed hover duration, a persistent dust floor (so the dust is always scattered rather than blinking on/off), and mobile scaling:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"043O4H4nbdY","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/index.html","replacements":[{"oldString":"          <defs>\n            <linearGradient id=\"arcGold\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n              <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"rgba(229,193,88,0.95)\" />\n              <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"rgba(201,162,39,0.3)\" />\n            </linearGradient>\n          </defs>\n          <circle class=\"arc arc-1\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"150\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"\n            stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"200 742\" opacity=\"0.6\" />\n          <circle class=\"arc arc-2\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"205\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\"\n            stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"120 1168\" opacity=\"0.35\" />\n          <circle class=\"arc arc-3\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"100\" stroke=\"url(#arcGold)\" stroke-width=\"1\"\n            stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"110 518\" opacity=\"0.45\" />","newString":"          <defs>\n            <linearGradient id=\"arcGoldHero\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n              <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"rgba(229,193,88,0.95)\" />\n              <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"rgba(201,162,39,0.3)\" />\n            </linearGradient>\n          </defs>\n          <circle class=\"arc arc-1\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"150\" stroke=\"url(#arcGoldHero)\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"\n            stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"200 742\" opacity=\"0.6\" />\n          <circle class=\"arc arc-2\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"17