ty. The `dust-float` animation is for the dots; wisps should use `dust-billow` for the soft breathing/rolling look.\n\nAlso de-glow:\n- `.ambient-dust`: width 4px, box-shadow: 0 0 6px 1px rgba(...,0.25) (much subtler), keyframes opacity peaks 0.65 → 0.5, 0.3 → 0.18.\n- `.sand-grain`: width 4px, box-shadow: 0 0 5px 1px rgba(...,0.25), sand-drift peak opacity 0.6 → 0.45, mid 0.3 → 0.2.\n\nHmm, but should I remove glow entirely? The bull's own ember/sparks glow — that's the impact focal point, keeping the balance. The scattered stuff should be subdued so the bull stays the focal point. So reducing glow significantly (not removing entirely) is right — they're dust, not LEDs.\n\nAlso the hero-ground haze is fine (soft). The vertical light beam mentioned in the screenshot — there's apparently a light beam shining on the bull (`hero-visual::after` maybe). That's existing, leave it.\n\nLet me also reduce the number of glowing dots: ambient-dust 9 → maybe keep 9 but de-glow. sand-grain 12 → keep but de-glow. That's fine.\n\nImplementation:\n\nHTML edits (index.html):\n1. In `.hero-content .hero-ambient`, add wisps. Currently:\n```html\n        <div class=\"hero-ambient\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <span class=\"ambient-dust\" ...>x9\n        </div>\n```\nAdd after the last ambient-dust span:\n```html\n          <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:34%;height:30%;left:-4%;top:22%;animation-delay:0s;\"></span>\n          <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:26%;height:24%;left:64%;top:44%;animation-delay:3.5s;\"></span>\n          <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:22%;height:20%;left:22%;top:66%;animation-delay:6.8s;\"></span>\n```\n\n2. In `.hero-ground`, add wisps after the haze divs:\n```html\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:30%;height:26%;left:8%;bottom:26%;animation-delay:1.2s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:24%;height:22%;left:34%;bottom:34%;animation-delay:4.6s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:36%;height:30%;left:56%;bottom:30%;animation-delay:2.4s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:20%;height:18%;left:88%;bottom:36%;animation-delay:5.8s;\"></span>\n```\nWait, hero-ground has height 46% and overflow hidden, positioned at bottom. Wisps at bottom:% of hero-ground. OK.\n\nActually, for wisps in hero-ground, since haze already covers the ground, maybe place wisps slightly higher (mid-height of the ground zone). bottom 26-40%. Fine.\n\nCSS edits (style.css):\n1. Add `.hero-wisp` rule + note it reuses dust-billow. Place it near the hero-ground block (after sand-drift keyframes).\n2. De-glow `.ambient-dust`: box-shadow and keyframes (dust-float opacity peaks).\n3. De-glow `.sand-grain`: box-shadow and sand-drift keyframes.\n\nAlso the `dust-billow` keyframes are defined under `.hero-visual` section — it's global, fine to reuse.\n\nWait, one issue: `.hero-content .hero-ambient` has `inset: 0; overflow: hidden;` — wisps inside will be clipped, good. And `.hero-content` children (eyebrow, h1, etc.) have z-index 1, ambient z-index 0 — wisps behind text. Good.\n\nAnother consideration — the wisp at left:-4% might clip. Fine.\n\nLet me make the edits. I'll do the HTML edit and CSS edit in one str_replace each.\n\nFor dust-float keyframes (used by ambient-dust), I need to lower opacity:\n```\n@keyframes dust-float {\n  0% { transform: translate(0,0) scale(0.6); opacity: 0; }\n  20% { opacity: 0.5; }\n  60% { opacity: 0.18; }\n  100% { transform: translate(14px,-110px) scale(1.25); opacity: 0; }\n}\n```\n\nFor sand-drift:\n```\n@keyframes sand-drift {\n  0% { transform: translate(0,0) scale(0.6); opacity: 0; }\n  18% { opacity: 0.45; }\n  55% { opacity: 0.18; }\n  100% { transform: translate(18px,-130px) scale(1.2); opacity: 0; }\n}\n```\n\nAnd sizes: ambient-dust 5px→4px with box-shadow 0 0 6px 1.5px rgba(201,162,39,0.22). sand-grain 5px→4px, box-shadow 0 0 5px 1px rgba(201,162,39,0.2).\n\nLet me write the edits now.","open":false,"collapse