ess down from 0.65 → 0.5\n- **Sand grains** (full-width ground): same treatment — 4px, faint 5px halo, peak 0.45\n\nThe specks now read as *dust catching light* rather than glowing LEDs. The only bright glow left is around the bull itself (its embers/sparks) — so the bull stays the focal point and the scattered atmosphere sits quietly around it, which restores the balance. Braces verified (442/442), wisps live in the DOM.\n\nReload the homepage — the dust should now feel like one soft storm blanketing the hero, with the bull glowing at its heart. If the wisps are still too present or too faint, I can tune their opacity in one rule. 🌪️"},{"kind":"tool","id":"1geML3nIqqo","toolName":"suggest_prompts","input":{"prompts":[{"prompt":"The balanced dust looks great — can you also soften the vertical light beam / other glow effects near the bull so nothing else competes with the dust storm?","label":"Soften remaining hero glows"},{"prompt":"Add a couple of large, very faint dust wisps that drift slowly across the whole hero in the background (like distant haze) for extra depth.","label":"Add distant drifting haze"},{"prompt":"Carry the same soft dust-wisp treatment into the sections below the hero so the whole homepage flows as one continuous atmosphere.","label":"Carry dust wisps down the page"}]}},{"kind":"changes","id":"p10-c9a80630","files":[{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\css\\style.css","status":"modified","lockfile":false,"binary":false,"adds":25,"dels":10,"patch":"Index: REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\css\\style.css\n===================================================================\n--- REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\css\\style.css\tbefore\n+++ REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-\\css\\style.css\tafter\n@@ -453,11 +453,11 @@\n \r\n .hero-content .ambient-dust {\r\n   position: absolute;\r\n-  width: 5px;\r\n-  height: 5px;\r\n+  width: 4px;\r\n+  height: 4px;\r\n   border-radius: 50%;\r\n   background: var(--accent-gold-light);\r\n-  box-shadow: 0 0 9px 2.5px rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.5);\r\n+ 