d (non-circular), darker/muted gold or grey-toned pebbles that sit/rest on the ground and/or drift, giving a \"debris\" feel from the bull's charge. Rocks should be more grounded — maybe static or barely-moving pebbles along the ground, plus a few that tumble slightly.\n\nDesign:\n- Add a new element class `.hero-rock` — small irregular pebbles (e.g., 7-11px, slightly rounded-square with border-radius variations, muted gold/dark gold color like rgba(160,130,60) with subtle top-light), scattered along the full-width ground in `.hero-ground`. Some can have a gentle \"hop\" or tumble animation (small bounce), but keep subtle. Most should feel static on the ground (grounded debris) with occasional drift — to keep balance and not look like glowing dots, rocks should NOT glow (no box-shadow or minimal).\n- Add more sand grains: increase count in `.hero-ground` from 12 → ~20, and maybe a few in `.hero-content` too. Also could add sand grains to `.hero-visual` already has 12; leave.\n\nAlso make sand/rocks feel part of \"the whole site\" — they said \"around the design\" — the hero is the main area. I'll focus on the hero (that's where the bull's dust is). Adding to other sections might be scope creep; the screenshot shows only the hero. The request: \"add more sand and mini rocks around the design to make the bulls dust feel a part of the whole site\" — the hero design. I'll enrich the hero ground layer.\n\nPlan:\n1. HTML `.hero-ground`: add ~8 more sand grains (total ~20) + ~8 mini rocks scattered across the width at ground level.\n2. CSS: add `.hero-rock` styling — irregular pebble look:\n   - size: vary via inline styles (width/height 6-12px)\n   - border-radius: 40% 60% 55% 45% / 55% 45% 60% 40% (organic)\n   - background: linear-gradient or solid muted gold — a darker, earthy gold like #8a6d2f / rgba(201,162,39,0.5), with subtle inset highlight to look 3D:\n     background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(214,170,70,0.75), rgba(120,90,30,0.75));\n   - no glow (or tiny)\n   - some get a gentle `rock-tumble` animation (small rotation + slight rise) with slow long durations; others static (animation none) to feel grounded.\n   - pointer-events none, z-index within hero-ground (below grid z-2).\n\nSince rocks sit at bottom of hero-ground (which is 46% of hero height), position them bottom 4-18% with varied lefts. A few \"mid-air\" rocks tossed up (bottom 25-35%) with tumble animation for the charge feel.\n\nLet me also add a few rocks to `.hero-content`? No — rocks on the ground is more natural. Keep rocks in hero-ground. Sand grains: add more in hero-ground.\n\nImplementation:\n\nHTML — extend `.hero-ground` div. Current content:\n```html\n    <div class=\"hero-ground\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <div class=\"hero-ground-haze\"></div>\n      <div class=\"hero-ground-haze hero-ground-haze-2\"></div>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:30%;height:28%;left:6%;bottom:30%;animation-delay:1.2s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:26%;height:24%;left:34%;bottom:40%;animation-delay:4.6s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:38%;height:32%;left:54%;bottom:34%;animation-delay:2.4s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"hero-wisp\" style=\"width:22%;height:20%;left:86%;bottom:42%;animation-delay:5.8s;\"></span>\n      <span class=\"sand-grain\" style=\"left:4%;bottom:12%;animation-delay:0s;\"></span>\n      ... 12 grains ...\n      <span class=\"sand-grain\" style=\"left:88%;bottom:27%;animation-delay:0.4s;\"></span>\n    </div>\n```\n\nI'll add 8 more sand grains and 8-10 rocks. Let me insert after the last sand-grain (left:88%;bottom:27%).\n\nNew grains (positions that don't clash too much — more mid-field):\n- left:9%; bottom:20%; delay:2.2s\n- left:18%; bottom:30%; delay:4.0s\n- left:32%; bottom:22%; delay:6.1s\n- left:43%; bottom:32%; delay:1.7s\n- left:55%; bottom:25%; delay:3.5s\n- left:67%; bottom:32%; delay:5.3s\n- left:78%; bottom:23%; delay:0.9s\n- left:96%; bottom:26%; delay:2.9s\n\nRocks (class hero-rock, inline width/height/left/bottom + optional rotation & tumble delay):\n- Grounded pebbles (no animation, or very slow settle):\n  - left:3%; bottom:8%; w 10px h 8px\n  - left:12%; bottom:6%; w 7px h 6px\n  - left:21%; bottom:10%; w 11px h 9px\n  - left:29%; bottom:5%; w 6px h 6px\n  - left:37%; bottom:9%; w 9px h 7px\n  - left:47%; bottom:7%; w 12px h 9px\n  - left:57%; bottom:11%; w 8px h 7px\n  - left:66%; bottom:6%; w 10px h 8px\n  - left:75%; bottom:9%; w 7px h 6px\n  - left:84%; bottom:5%; w 11px h 9px\n  - left:92%; bottom:8%; w 8px h 7px\n- A few tossed-up rocks (tumble animation, mid-air):\n  - left:15%; bottom:26%; w 9px h 7px; tumble\n  - left:40%; bottom:30%; w 7px h 6px; tumble delay 2s\n  - left:60%; bottom:28%; w 10px h 8px; tumble delay 4s\n  - left:80%; bottom:30%; w 6px h 6px; tumble delay 1s\n\nThat's 15 rocks total — maybe a bit many. Let me do 11 grounded + 4 airborne = 15. Actually \"more sand and mini rocks\" — they want it clearly present. 12-15 rocks fine. Let me do 12 grounded + 3 airborne = 15? Hmm, keep it reasonable: 10 grounded pebbles + 4 tossed rocks = 14. Fine.\n\nActually, let me moderate: 9 grounded + 3 airborne = 12 rocks. Plus 8 more grains → 20 grains total.\n\nCSS:\n```css\n.hero-ground .hero-rock {\n  position: absolute;\n  border-radius: 42% 58% 52% 48% / 54% 46% 58% 42%;\n  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(212, 175, 90, 0.55), rgba(110, 85, 32, 0.65));\n  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(255, 220, 150, 0.25), 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);\n  opacity: 0.85;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n\n.hero-ground .hero-rock.tossed {\n  animation: rock-tumble 9s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n\n@keyframes rock-tumble {\n  0%, 100% { transform: rotate(0deg) translateY(0); opacity: 0.85; }\n  15% { opacity: 0.7; }\n  45% { transform: rotate(120deg) translateY(-34px); opacity: 0.5; }\n  75% { transform: rotate(240deg) translateY(-8px); opacity: 0.75; }\n}\n```\n\nWait — for the tossed rocks, they start on the ground and hop up? The animation translateY(-34px) at 45% then back down — like a pebble kicked up. Good. Rotate for tumble.\n\nFor grounded pebbles: no animation, static. But a static rock layer is nice to ground the scene. opacity 0.85 static.\n\nMobile: scale rocks down (add to the 968px media query): `.hero-ground .hero-rock { width: ... }` — inline widths are set, so instead reduce opacity/size via transform: scale(0.8). Simpler: add `.hero-ground .hero-rock { transform: scale(0.75); }` in media query — but that conflicts with tossed animation transform. Hmm. For mobile, keep it simple — just leave as is; inline sizes in px are small enough (6-12px). Rocks fine on mobile.\n\nActually wait — one issue: `.hero-rock` z-index. hero-ground is z-index 1, its children stack in DOM order. The scroll-indicator is outside hero-ground so it's above. Fine.\n\nAlso sand grains are 5px glow dots; rocks 6-12px muted earthy. Good contrast.\n\nLet me write the HTML edit (insert after last sand-grain) and CSS edit (append rock styles after sand-drift keyframes, before the mobile media query — actually there's a media query right after; I'll insert before `/* Mobile — scale the ground dust down with the bull */`).\n\nLet me get the exact current text around the last sand-grain to anchor the insert. From my earlier edit, the grains end with:\n`<span class=\"sand-grain\" style=\"left:88%;bottom:27%;animation-delay:0.4s;\"></span>`\nfollowed by `\\n    </div>`.\n\nI'll insert the new grains + rocks between that and `</div>`.\n\nCSS anchor: the `@keyframes sand-drift` block ends with `}` then blank line then `/* Mobile — scale the ground dust down with the bull */`. I'll insert rock CSS before the mobile comment.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"ad","id":"p2-711c1f99","ad":{"adText":"ZoomInfo FormComplete boosts your lead quality and conversion rates by automatically enriching and verifying web form submissions in real-time.","title":"ZoomInfo FormComplete","cta":"Lear