aligned within the container.\n\nThe user wants \"the whole text properly centered\". So they want the text block centered on the page (horizontally centered as a column), and probably the text itself centered too.\n\nCurrent state:\n- `.hero-grid`: single column grid, content fills width, left-aligned.\n- `.hero-content`: max-width 650px, text left-aligned within.\n\nThe screenshot \"shows exactly why this text isn't centered\" — likely the text is sitting at the left with lots of empty space on the right (because the container is full-width but content is left aligned, OR the content box starts at the container's left edge and the text block is narrow).\n\nTo center: \n- Center the `.hero-content` block itself in the grid: `justify-self: center; margin: 0 auto;` \n- And center the text: `text-align: center` on hero-content.\n\nBut wait — the hero has the image as background with the bull on the right. If we center the text, it'll overlay the middle/bull area. Earlier the user wanted text on the LEFT over the image (\"adding the game changer side on top of it\" — with the image having negative space on the left). Now they say \"center the whole text properly\".\n\nThe screenshot presumably shows the text block pushed left (maybe because the grid column is full width and content is left-aligned, looking off-center). The user wants it centered.\n\nHmm, but they previously wanted it on the left side over the image. Now they're asking to center it. Let me trust the current request: center the text block and its contents.\n\nApproach:\n- `.hero-grid`: add `justify-content: center` isn't needed; make the single grid column content centered: `.hero-content { justify-self: center; text-align: center; }` — and maybe reduce max-width for a tidy centered column (e.g., keep 650px or 720px).\n- The CTA buttons row (`.hero-ctas`) — with text-align center, the flex row should also center: `.hero-ctas { justify-content: center; }`.\n- The ambient dust positions are percentage-based within hero-content — they'll shift with the content box; fine.\n\nLet me check the current hero-content CSS to edit precisely. From earlier:\n```css\n.hero-content {\n  max-width: 650px;\n  position: relative;\n}\n```\nAnd `.hero-ctas { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }`.\n\nAlso the eyebrow/h1 etc. inherit text-align from parent.\n\nPlan:\n```css\n.hero-content {\n  max-width: 720px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  text-align: center;\n  position: relative;\n}\n.hero-ctas {\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n```\n\nWait — should the whole text block be centered or just centered within the container? \"center the whole text properly\" — center both the block and the text. I'll do both: block centered via margin auto (or justify-self center in grid), and text center-aligned.\n\nAlso, since the hero is now a background image with the bull likely on the right, centered text might overlap the bull. But the user asked for it explicitly after seeing the screenshot, so do it. If the image has the bull on the right and darker space center/left, centered text over the middle could still be readable with the shade. The mobile shade already handles small screens.\n\nHmm — but actually, should I keep the shade left-weighted? The shade is `linear-gradient(90deg, dark left → transparent right)`. If text is centered, a left-heavy shade means the center/right text sits over a lighter area. I should adjust the shade to be a broader center-weighted scrim so the centered text is readable: e.g., `radial-gradient(ellipse at 35% 50%, rgba(5,5,5,0.72), transparent 70%)` or a center-heavy linear gradient. Let me update the shade to a centered radial so text pops regardless of position.\n\nLet me make the shade:\n```css\n.hero-shade {\n  background:\n    radial-gradient(ellipse at 38% 50%, rgba(5, 5, 5, 0.75) 0%, rgba(5, 5, 5, 0.35) 45%, transparent 75%);\n}\n```\nHmm, but the bull on the right should stay visible. A radial centered at ~38% keeps right side clear-ish. On mobile keep the vertical gradient (already there).\n\nActually, let me keep it simpler and effective: center the text block with margin auto + text-align center, and make the shade slightly stronger toward the center-left where text now sits. I'll use a radial gradient at 40% 50%.\n\nWait — but do I know the text will be centered over the image nicely? The user explicitly wants centered text. Go with it.\n\nAlso — one more consideration: the h1 \"Game Changers\" is large; centered is fine.\n\nMobile: text centered on mobile too — with vertical shade, readable.\n\nEdits:\n1. `.hero-content`: add margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; (keep max-width 650px → maybe 720px for balance).\n2. `.hero-ctas`: add justify-content: center.\n3. `.hero-shade`: change to center-weighted radial so centered text is readable.\n\nLet me apply.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"ad","id":"p2-2273661e","ad":{"adText":"Elevate your home bar aesthetic with Barillio’s pro-level, rustproof stainless-steel cocktail tools.","title":"Upgrade Your Home Bar with Professional Barillio Tools","cta":"Shop Barillio","url":"https://www.barillio-barware.com/shop/?aff=114","favicon":"https://icons.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.barillio-barware.com.ico","clickUrl":"https://api.trygravity.ai/track/click?p=gAAAAABqdE25Al4cILDiOs37xvDQvUN1lHug3Yr759OUZHXIBkzFZQgvI8-0Ek7iMIQsstXgdrPekx6WMPlL5Ro2JWH69BwY2BiJ3Fu6BAQxVyO9hdogqq6KknPdYCDVg2BHBXXGVjWkBa6gVBFw3LC8Sm0Vyp3Mq9IWVka5ZXLt0LcAvhFgZMUK_RC-V8uTJSQFrmyhKuFHIZUxNub0MRrhVUo4HlB2UNtchlfPFNx-JL6xNRkOLtlmKjbXE564tlpccdfuyToPYn10815j5LPV4Lv80HJprrg0SeXIO7zYSCkhGeZ5q31EvJxSuVHESNS2JS_K2CheYLMCKocewX6YZZqazq3ZNV1dqWSb1BlOR3rWkKI6kJqTlO5q9m51I9O2z7tiFQVNuUfWuMQ_OCVsaE0TrsM-kD_-q2im2VjBGOvVYTZC-70Q2rLVI-59Y9KVI7mtVS3Vsy_2isfs289Nsj0eA1BkgId3i_nI6B94O9LPNZHxbB-bREEQ0VO_8WkOLFlN2Q8Ix_drq1uj8sbUaBxzkxdc9d0i-maxeuFLU9zoO-an8l8KMdVkZlqUUQr-e3Cel6yOSI1zN-c98iYGmiAT3uZ8H3yxJdYBp0WcDU_E1lAU4UgP5abqb2uBYwVwUNHcZAartLzidUuXOme0YeUisjkVdznla-Bo2XLmJ9cXn2uh2ygjs6dyrdB-2Tv