 I Started Reality FX is correct though don't touch that\" — they consider the headings correct. But the paragraphs/signature sit 3.5px left of the headings. That's EXACTLY the \"not in the center fully\" complaint from before, now resolved differently:\n\nThe user wants everything aligned on ONE axis. Since they say the headings are correct (don't touch), the fix is to REMOVE my -0.2em transform from the paragraphs and signature so they align exactly with the headings and \"By The Numbers\".\n\nBut wait — the -0.2em was MY optical correction for the italic lean. If I remove it, the italic text goes back to being optically shifted right (the complaint that started this). Hmm. But the user now says the headings are correct and everything should align WITH them. The headings are upright (not italic) — the italic letter paragraphs inherently lean right relative to the headings. There's a physical conflict: italic text's glyph centers vs upright text's glyph centers.\n\nHmm wait, actually — let me reconsider. The -0.2em transform shifts the LAYOUT box left. For italic text, the glyph ink extends right of the layout box. My transform moves the box left by 0.2em so glyph ink centers on the page axis. That's the optical correction. If I REMOVE it, the italic glyph ink sits right of center by ~3.5px → misaligned with headings by 3.5px the OTHER way.\n\nThe user wants everything on the same axis. The headings are the reference. So the question: does the user perceive the italic letter as aligned with the heading WITH the -0.2em correction or not?\n\nThe user's previous message: \"the text moved more to the right but it's not in the center fully yet\" — they wanted it moved LEFT more (further toward center). I added -0.2em (left shift). Now they say the headings are correct and the letter should align with them. \n\nIf the user now says headings are correct and everything else should align with them, and if my -0.2em made the letter align with the headings, then the user woul