n4. **The ticker** — overflow hidden ✓.\n5. **The index hero on mobile** — the hero-shade mobile override exists ✓ (added earlier).\n6. **The mobile menu** — `.mobile-menu.open` — verify it works.\n7. **The evaluation/contact forms** — form fields full width.\n8. **The meter-grid** — min-width 90px on mobile ✓.\n9. **value-grid/benefit-grid/card-grid** — auto-fit minmax stacks ✓.\n10. **Emoji icons** — the user earlier wanted professional emojis — done previously.\n11. **job-head flex column at 640px** ✓ (saw it).\n\nLet me check the timeline and pricing grids and the form steps quickly. Also — one REAL mobile concern I should double check: the **`.ticker-strip`** and **TradingView widget** on index — fine.\n\nAnd **the `.stats-grid`** with minmax(180px, 1fr) — on a 421px screen: 180px min → 2 columns of ~195px each. Fine.\n\n**The `.card-grid`** minmax(300px, 1fr) → on 421px, 1 column (since 300×2 + gap > 421). Fine.\n\n**The pricing/program grids** — let me check what grid they use. Let me look at the programs page structure + its grid CSS.\n\nAlso the **timeline** on careers.\n\nLet me check these two + the multi-step form behavior. Also let me verify the `.mobile-menu` CSS and the `.form-step` CSS.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"All 8 pages pass the HTML-level overflow check. Now let me statically verify the remaining mobile-sensitive components — the careers timeline, program pricing grids, and multi-step form states:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"1oyl686HFmY","toolName":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"grep -n -A12 '^\\.timeline' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -30; echo '===== pricing grid:'; grep -n -B2 -A6 'pricing-grid\\|plan-grid\\|program-grid\\|package-grid' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -30; echo '===== form-step:'; grep -n -A6 '^\\.form-step' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -16","process_type":"SYNC","timeout_seconds":30}},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p26-69d9921b","text":"- Timeline: max-width 720px, centered, left-aligned rail — mobile-safe ✓\n- No pricing-grid CSS found. Let me check what the programs page uses — probably `.card-grid` or a custom class. Let me check the programs.html structure.\n- form-step: display none until .active — and main.js `if (formSteps.length > 0) showFormStep(0);` — sets step 0 active on load ✓. And now with the `.js` gating + safety net, even if JS breaks, the FIRST step would... hmm wait — `.form-step` is `display: none` by CSS, NOT gated behind .js! If JS fails, ALL form steps stay hidden! The forms would be invisible!\n\nThe user said \"any other inaccuracies on mobile\" — but this is a bigger issue: forms hidden without JS (on ANY device). Let me fix the form-step CSS the same way: gate behind `.js`:\n\n```css\n.form-step { display: none; }\n.form-step.active { display: block; }\n```\nbecomes:\n```css\n.js .form-step { display: none; }\n.js .form-step.active { display: block; }\n```\n\nWait — but if JS works, the first step gets `.active` on load. If JS fails, with the gating, ALL steps show stacked (ugly but visible). Hmm — showing ALL steps stacked is not great either. But visible content > invisible forms for launch. Actually — for a multi-step form, showing all steps at once without JS is genuinely broken UX (the user would see a jumble of fields). But at least they'd see the form exists. Hmm.\n\nActually — let me reconsider. The forms are the contact/careers/evaluation forms. If JS fails, with gating the form shows all steps stacked = messy but functional-ish (they could still fill and submit... actually the submit handler is JS too, so submit wouldn't work without JS — but Formspree forms work WITHOUT JS via native POST! The `action=\"https://formspree.io/f/xxx\"` — without the JS submit handler, the browser does a native POST to Formspree and redirects to Formspree's success page. That WORKS — the user leaves the site, but the submission arrives. That's the pre-existing fallback!).\n\nSo with the `.js` gating on form-steps: JS broken → all steps visible → user fills them → native Formspree POST works. Acceptable fallback.\n\nHmm, but actually — is it worth touching? The user's report is about the careers listings. The form-steps display:none is a real risk though (if JS stalls, no form appears anywhere — that would look broken at launch). Let me gate it behind .js too for safety. Low risk, real benefit.\n\nWait, actually — let me check how many forms use form-steps: careers has 2 forms (job application + talent pool), evaluation has 1, contact has 1. Let me check which pages use `.form-step`. The multi-step logic: `if (formSteps.length > 0) showFormStep(0)` shows step 0 on load. So with JS running, step 1 shows. Fine.\n\nLet me apply the `.js` gate to `.form-step` as well.\n\nNow the programs page grid — let me check programs.html structure for the plan cards.\n\nAlso — let me check the `.mobile-menu` CSS — is it `display: none` and `.open` shows it? If mobile-menu is hidden by default and only shown via JS toggling `.open`, then without JS the hamburger does nothing — fine (hamburger hidden at desktop widths anyway; at mobile widths without JS the menu is just not accessible — acceptable, though the links are in the footer anyway).\n\nLet me check mobile-menu CSS.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"The timeline is mobile-safe, but I found a real risk: `.form-step { display: none }` — if JS stalls, **all multi-step forms stay invisible** (same class of bug as the listings). Let me gate it too, and check the mobile-menu and programs grid:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"1ozjVm1vAy8","toolName":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"grep -n -A10 '^\\.mobile-menu' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -26; echo '===== programs page plans:'; grep -n 'plan\\|package\\|card' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/programs.html | head -12; echo '===== .form-step usage pages:'; grep -ln 'form-step' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/*.html","process_type":"SYNC","timeout_seconds":30}},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p27-69d9921b","text":"Key findings:\n1. **`.mobile-menu`** — WAIT, this is a PROBLEM! The mobile-menu base styles: let me see the full block. Lines 358-379 show `.mobile-menu` with `display: flex` but what's the initial opacity/visibility? Let me see lines 358-379 fully. The snippet shows:\n```\n.mobile-menu {\n  position: fixed;\n  ...\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  ...(cut)\n}\n.mobile-menu.open {\n  opacity: 1;\n  pointer-events: all;\n}\n```\nThere must be `opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;` in the base — let me check. If the base has opacity 0 + pointer-events none, and `.open` shows it — that's JS-driven. Without JS, the mobile menu stays hidden — acceptable (footer has links).\n\n2. **`.form-step` is used ONLY on evaluation.html** — so the multi-step form is the evaluation form. The careers/contact forms are single-step (no form-step). So gating `.form-step` behind `.js` affects only evaluation.html. Let me apply the gate.\n\n3. **Programs page uses `.program-card`** — 7 cards, one is `featured`. Let me check the `.program-card` grid CSS for mobile stacking. Let me look at the `.program-card` CSS + its container grid.\n\nLet me check the mobile-menu base opacity and the program-card CSS.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"tool","id":"1o0IagkSCXM","toolName":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"sed -n '358,378p' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css; echo '===== program-card:'; grep -n -B3 -A8 'program-card' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -40; echo '===== program grid container:'; grep -n -B2 -A6 'programs-grid\\|program-grid\\|plans-grid' REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/css/style.css | head -20","process_type":"SYNC","timeout_seconds":30}},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p28-69d9921b","text":"- `.mobile-menu`: opacity 0 + pointer-events none, `.open` shows it. JS-driven but the base state is hidden — safe (menu hidden without JS is acceptable; footer links still navi