er the careers page listings issue ONE more time to be sure I've fully addressed the reported bug:\n\nThe user reported: on mobile, Open Positions job listings not showing. My analysis: the `.reveal` system starts content at opacity:0; if the IntersectionObserver didn't fire on their mobile browser, the listings stayed invisible. My fixes:\n1. `.js .reveal` gating — content VISIBLE by default; only hidden once JS confirms running. Even if the observer never fires, the safety net + threshold 0 handle it, AND if JS is entirely broken, content is visible (no .js class → no hidden state).\n2. threshold 0 (was 0.1) — fires for any pixel of visibility, reliable for tall sections.\n3. Scroll safety net — reveals anything on screen if the observer stalls.\n4. No-IO fallback — shows everything on old browsers.\n\nThis comprehensively fixes the listings bug. Plus the evaluation form got the same protection.\n\nNow let me also make sure I haven't broken anything with the `.js` gating — specifically: the reveal elements that are ABOVE the fold on page load (e.g., hero content). With threshold 0, they reveal immediately on load (observer fires since they intersect). The `.js` class is added synchronously at DOMContentLoaded — before first paint? DOMContentLoaded fires after parsing; the .js class gets added then. There could be a brief flash where content is visible (before .js added) then hidden then re-revealed. Actually no: the sequence is — CSS loads (content visible, no .js), DOM parses, DOMContentLoaded fires → .js added (content hides for above-fold reveals) → observer fires immediately (they intersect) → .visible added (content shows with animation). So there's a tiny hide-then-animate-in on load for above-fold content. That's the same as before (before, above-fold content was hidden from the start until the observer fired ~instantly). Fine.\n\nOne more consideration — the `.reveal` elements that are mid-page: previously they were hidden until scrolled to. Now the same. 