"id":"1yd0TMJJ4TM","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"Systeme.io free plan limits students contacts products funnels 2025 2026","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yeBaDGKAII","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"Teachable free plan transaction fees Thinkific free plan limits Kajabi free trial 2025 2026","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yeTZZ2cRIc","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"Kajabi free trial length 2025 2026","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yeT_eq4CHo","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"embed course player custom domain login vs platform login Thinkific Teachable Systeme","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yeUexCOSJA","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"Firebase Authentication free tier limits Firestore free tier limits Supabase free tier limits 2025 2026","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yesnVFzEXo","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://systeme.io/pricing","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yesv1j5nkU","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://www.teachable.com/pricing","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yetJcMDiRs","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://supabase.com/pricing","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yetuMd4uV0","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/quotas","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"tool","id":"1yetuZVpdVs","toolName":"read_url","input":{"url":"https://www.podia.com/pricing","max_chars":20000}},{"kind":"text","text":"Here is a comprehensive 2025–2026 research breakdown comparing the pricing, free tiers, video hosting, domain capabilities, and backend auth options for launching a small forex education business on a limited budget.\n\n---\n\n### Part 1: Course & Membership Platform Comparison\n\n#### 1. **Podia**\n* **Free Plan Limits:** **Podia retired its permanent free plan.** They no longer offer a free tier. \n* **Free Trial:** A **30-day free trial** is available for their paid plans (no credit card required upfront).\n* **Paid Plan Pricing & Limits (2025–2026):**\n  * *Mover Plan:* $49/month ($39–$42/mo billed annually) + a **5% transaction fee**. Includes 50 products and 25 community spaces.\n  * *Shaker Plan:* $99/month ($75–$84/mo billed annually) with **0% transaction fees**. Includes unlimited products and community spaces.\n  * *Earthquaker Plan:* $150–$179/month billed annually with 0% transaction fees and unlimited everything.\n\n#### 2. **Systeme.io** (The Best True Budget Option)\n* **Free Plan Limits:** Systeme.io is one of the only major all-in-one platforms still offering a permanent, feature-complete free tier with no time limit:\n  * **Contacts / Students:** Up to **2,000 contacts** and **500 students**.\n  * **Sales Funnels:** Up to **3 sales funnels** (with up to 10 funnel steps).\n  * **Products / Courses:** Up to **1 online course** / 1 digital store / 3 products.\n  * **Email Marketing:** **Unlimited** email sends.\n  * **Transaction Fees:** **0%** platform transaction fees (you only pay standard Stripe/PayPal processing fees).\n  * **Custom Domain:** Supports **1 custom domain** on the free tier.\n* **Paid Plans:** *Startup* ($17/mo) increases limits to 5,000 contacts and 5 courses; *Webinar* ($47/mo) covers 10,000 contacts.\n\n#### 3. **Teachable**\n* **Free Plan Limits:** **Teachable retired its free plan.** \n* **Transaction Fees:** \n  * *Starter Plan* ($39/mo monthly or $29/mo annually): Features a steep **7.5% transaction fee** on sales via Teachable Payments.\n  * *Builder Plan* ($89/mo monthly or $69/mo annually) and higher: **0% transaction fees**.\n* **Other Starter Limits:** Capped at **5 products**, 1 admin user, and 100 active students (limits lift once you pass $10k/year in direct platform sales).\n* **Free Trial:** Includes a **7-day free trial** and a 30-day money-back guarantee.\n\n#### 4. **Thinkific**\n* **Free Plan Limits:** **Thinkific has eliminated its free plan.** \n* **Paid Plan Pricing:** Starts with the *Start* plan at **$99/month** (or ~$74/month billed annually). \n* **Student/Product Limits:** Offers **unlimited students** and unlimited courses even on entry-level paid plans. There are **0% platform transaction fees** in the US/most regions.\n* **Free Trial:** Provides a **30-day free trial** of the full platform.\n\n#### 5. **Kajabi**\n* **Free Plan Limits:** **No free plan exists.** Kajabi is built for scaling businesses and is the most expensive option.\n* **Pricing:** *Basic* plan starts at **$179/month** ($143/mo billed annually), capping you at 2,500 contacts and 5 products. The *Growth* plan is $249/month.\n* **Free Trial:** Standard trial is **14 days**, though partner/promotional links commonly offer **30 days** or special entry promotions (e.g., 3 months for $99).\n\n---\n\n### Part 2: Custom Domains, Course Embedding, and Student Login Architecture\n\n* **Can you embed the course player on your own custom domain?**\n  * **No traditional hosted course builder** (Thinkific, Teachable, Podia, Kajabi, Systeme.io) lets you iframe or natively embed their course player dashboard onto an external third-party domain (e.g., your own WordPress or custom React site). \n  * **Why?** Security and session tracking. They require students to log into a branded portal hosted on their platform ecosystem (though you can map a custom subdomain like `members.yourforexbrand.com` to make it look native).\n* **Where do students log in?**\n  * Students must log in via the platform's authentication portal (using custom domains/subdomains you configure). If you want students logging in natively on your *own* web application frontend domain without ever touching a third-party portal URL, you cannot use these standard SaaS tools out-of-the-box—you would need a custom-built portal.\n\n---\n\n### Part 3: Video Hosting vs. YouTube Unlisted Embedding\n\n* **Included Video Hosting (Secure/Encrypted):**\n  * **Teachable, Thinkific, Kajabi, Podia, and Systeme.io** all include built-in, secure video hosting (powered by enterprise video infrastructure like Wistia, Vimeo Enterprise, or AWS) on their paid plans. Videos cannot be easily downloaded or hotlinked by non-students.\n* **YouTube Unlisted Embedding:**\n  * Some platforms allow you to embed YouTube unlisted videos directly into lessons. However, for a **forex education business**, this is a major security risk: unlisted YouTube links can easily be extracted via browser developer tools or browser extensions and leaked publicly across Telegram groups or forums, bypassing your membership paywall entirely.\n\n---\n\n### Part 4: Custom Portal Backend Option (Firebase vs. Supabase Free Tiers)\n\nIf you have developer capabilities and want to bypass high platform fees by building a lightweight custom student portal (e.g., React/Next.js frontend + backend database), here is how the free tiers stack up:\n\n#### 1. **Firebase (Google Cloud)**\n* **Authentication:** **Firebase Auth** is free for up to **50,000 Monthly Active Users (MAUs)** for standard email/password and social logins (Google, Apple, etc.). Phone/SMS auth has separate paid limits.\n* **Database (Cloud Firestore):** Generous permanent free quota:\n  * **Stored Data:** 1 GiB total.\n  * **Document Reads:** 50,000 reads per day.\n  * **Document Writes:** 20,000 writes per day.\n  * **Outbound Data Transfer:** 10 GiB per month.\n* *Verdict:* Extremely reliable and permanent free tier, but database queries can scale up quickly if your forex portal tracks real-time data or heavy user activity logs.\n\n#### 2. **Supabase (Open-Source Firebase Alternative)**\n* **Authentication:** **Supabase Auth** includes **50,000 Monthly Active Users (MAUs)** for free.\n* **Database (PostgreSQL):** \n  * **Database Size:** **500 MB** Postgres database storage.\n  * **API Requests:** **Unlimited** API requests.\n  * **Egress / Bandwidth:** 5 GB egress per month.\n  * **File Storage (for PDFs/materials):** 1 GB file storage.\n  * *Caveat:* Free projects are **paused after 1 week of complete inactivity**, requiring a manual resume in the dashboard (though easily automated or avoided with active traffic).\n* *Verdict:* Gives you a full relational **PostgreSQL** database (ideal if you prefer SQL over NoSQL Firestore) and generous request limits, though 500 MB database space requires keeping user logs lean."}]},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p3-401118bc","text":"Great research. Now let me write my response. Key facts:\n- Free tiers: Systeme.io (500 students, 1 course, 0% fees, custom domain) is the standout free option. Podia/Teachable/Thinkific killed free plans.\n- Hosted platforms require login on their portal (subdomain trick: members.yourdomain.com).\n- Video security: unlisted YouTube is leaky; platforms include secure video hosting.\n- Custom backend: Firebase/Supabase free tiers are generous but it's real engineering.\n\nNow write the honest assessment. Structure:\n\n1. Excitement + honesty about the one hard constraint: static site = no real backend. A real student portal needs 4 things: accounts/auth, gated content, progress, payments (later). Can't fake that with static HTML.\n2. Three paths:\n   - Path A: Hosted LMS (Systeme.io free tier standout) — recommend for launch\n   - Path B: Custom branded portal on Firebase/Supabase — the \"looks 100% like our site\" option, more engineering\n   - Path C: WordPress migration (their long-term plan)\n3. What I recommend: Hybrid — build the portal page/shell in our exact style, link from site \"Student Portal\" button; behind it either Systeme.io or a custom build. Also mention video security for their forex course content — this is important for them (course content = their business asset).\n4. Questions I need from them before we build: course format (videos/PDFs/mentor), how students pay (online card vs EFT — South Africa context), student numbers, and whether portal must live on realityfx domain.\n5. Then suggest_prompts.\n\nKeep it conversational, confident, struct