xtraction in background\n- While it runs: draft Chapter 1 answer key file, build OS app files\n- Check extraction results, verify counts\n- Register preview, test\n- Review\n\nLet me first write todos, then kick off extraction.\n\nFor extraction: \n```bash\nmkdir -p REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/assets/slides\ncd \"/c/Users/user/Downloads/Reality Forex Trading Full course pdfs\"\nfor f in *.pdf; do\n  ch=$(echo \"$f\" | sed -E 's/CHAPTER ([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\n  outdir=\"/c/.../REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/assets/slides/ch$ch\"\n  mkdir -p \"$outdir\"\n  pdftoppm -png -r 100 \"$f\" \"$outdir/slide\"\ndone\n```\npdftoppm outputs slide-01.png, slide-02.png... zero-padded by page number.\n\nWait — I should confirm the project structure. The project root is `C:\\Users\\user\\Downloads\\REALITY FX TRADING\\reality-fx-site` and the site lives in `REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-`. The blueprint I wrote went to `REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/REALITY-FX-OS-BLUEPRINT.md`. So the OS should live at `REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/`.\n\nAlso — 740 images at r=100. Nearpod exports are usually 16:9 slides. r=100 gives ~1600x900. Good enough for a lesson player. Could use r=110. Fine.\n\nLet me also consider: should I render only the non-quiz slides, or all? All — the lesson player will show content slides as images; quiz slides get replaced by interactive quizzes. Actually simpler: lesson player shows ALL slide images as pages in a scrollable/stepped viewer, and at known quiz positions inserts interactive quizzes. But mapping quiz positions requires knowing which PDF pages have quizzes. From the text extraction I know the page numbers (e.g., Ch1 quiz at page 11 of 22; Ch4 fill-blank at 84; Ch6 essay at 25; polls at 8-10, 47-48 etc.). I could encode \"interactive slide\" markers. For Ch1: content slides 1-7 (pages 1-7), poll page 8 (which trader — that's a great OS onboarding poll! keep as image or interactive?), poll 9-10 (self-assess), quiz 11-21, final 22.\n\nFor simplicity and speed: the lesson player shows s