-in, .tool-row, .tool-result, .tool-out, etc.\n\nLet me write renderLab:\n\n```js\nfunction renderLab(root) {\n  root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"page-head\", `\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Laboratory</p>\n    <h2>The Risk Laboratory</h2>\n    <p class=\"page-sub\">Practice the exact formulas from Chapter 7 — position sizing, R-multiples, and drawdown recovery. No real money required. This is where theory becomes instinct.</p>`));\n  const grid = el(\"div\", \"lab-grid\");\n  grid.appendChild(positionSizer());\n  grid.appendChild(rMultiple());\n  grid.appendChild(tradeOutcome());\n  grid.appendChild(drawdownRecovery());\n  root.appendChild(grid);\n}\n```\n\npositionSizer:\n```js\nfunction positionSizer() {\n  const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n  c.innerHTML = `\n    <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">⚖️</span><div><h3>Position Sizer</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">Net Liquidation × %Risk ÷ (Stop × $/pip)</p></div></div>\n    <div class=\"tool-in\">\n      <label>Account balance ($)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-balance\" value=\"1000\" min=\"0\"></label>\n      <label>Risk per trade (%)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-risk\" value=\"1\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" step=\"0.1\"></label>\n      <label>Stop loss (pips)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-stop\" value=\"20\" min=\"0\"></label>\n      <label>Pip value / standard lot ($)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-pip\" value=\"10\" min=\"0\" step=\"0.1\"></label>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"ps-result\">—</div>`;\n  const upd = () => {\n    const b = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-balance\").value || 0;\n    const r = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-risk\").value || 0;\n    const s = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-stop\").value || 0;\n    const p = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-pip\").value || 0;\n    const risk$ = b * r / 100;\n    const lots = (s > 0 && p > 0) ? risk$ / (s * p) : 0;\n    const res = c.querySelector(\"#ps-result\");\n    if (risk$ <= 0 || lots <= 0) { res.innerHTML = \"<span class='dim'>Enter your numbers above</span>\"; return; }\n    res.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"out-big\">${risk$.toFixed(2)} <small>USD at risk</small></div>\n      <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Standard lots</span><b>${lots.toFixed(2)}</b></div>\n      <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Mini lots</span><b>${(lots * 10).toFixed(1)}</b></div>\n      <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Micro lots (contracts)</span><b>${Math.round(lots * 100)}</b></div>`;\n  };\n  c.querySelectorAll(\"input\").forEach(i => i.addEventListener(\"input\", upd));\n  upd();\n  return c;\n}\n```\n\nrMultiple:\n```js\nfunction rMultiple() {\n  const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n  c.innerHTML = `\n    <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">🎯</span><div><h3>R:R Planner</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">How many R is your target worth?</p></div></div>\n    <div class=\"tool-in\">\n      <label>Entry price<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-entry\" value=\"1.1000\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n      <label>Stop loss<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-stop\" value=\"1.0900\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n      <label>Take profit<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-target\" value=\"1.1300\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n      <label>Direction<select id=\"rr-side\"><option value=\"long\">Long (buy)</option><option value=\"short\">Short (sell)</option></select></label>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"rr-result\">—</div>`;\n  const upd = () => {\n    const e = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-entry\").value || 0;\n    const s = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-stop\").value || 0;\n    const t = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-target\").value || 0;\n    const side = c.querySelector(\"#rr-side\").value;\n    const R = Math.abs(e - s);\n    const rr = R > 0 ? Math.abs(t - e) / R : 0;\n    const res = c.querySelector(\"#rr-result\");\n    if (!R) { res.innerHTML = \"<span class='dim'>Enter prices above</span>\"; return; }\n    const good = (side === \"long\" ? t > e : t < e);\n    res.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"out-big ${good ? \"\" : \"warn\"}\">1 : ${rr.toFixed(2)} <small>reward to risk</small></div>\n      <div class=\"out-row\"><span>1R distance</span><b>${R.toFixed(4)}</b></div>\n      ${good ? \"\" : \"<div class='warn-note'>Target is on the wrong side of entry — flip your direction or target.</div>\"}`;\n  };\n  ...\n}\n```\n\ntradeOutcome (R earned):\n```js\nentry, exit, stop, direction → outcomeR\n```\nActually to keep it tight, maybe combine into one card \"R earned\": entry, exit, stop, direction. Let me include it — it's cheap.\n\ndrawdownRecovery:\n```js\nloss % input → gain needed %; plus a mini table for the classic values.\n```\n\nCSS: .lab-grid { grid 2 cols }, .tool-card, .tool-head, .tool-ic, .tool-sub, .tool-in label styling, inputs, .tool-result, .out-big, .out-row, .warn, .warn-note, .dim. Mobile: single column.\n\nLet me write the edits. I'll add renderLab + helper functions into os.js (insert before \"/* ========== CERTIFICATE\" section), add the route case, and update index.html nav.\n\nLet me write the code carefully.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"Now building the Risk Calculator into the OS Laboratory. First the app logic:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"12Ae6Kd4diA","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/js/os.js","replacements":[{"oldString":"  /* ============================================================\n     CERTIFICATE\n     ============================================================ */","newString":"  /* ============================================================\n     LABORATORY — Risk Calculator\n     ============================================================ */\n  function renderLab(root) {\n    root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"page-head\", `\n      <p class=\"eyebrow\">Laboratory</p>\n      <h2>The Risk Laboratory</h2>\n      <p class=\"page-sub\">Practise the exact formulas from Chapter 7 — position sizing, R-multiples, and drawdown recovery. No real money required. This is where theory becomes instinct.</p>`));\n    const grid = el(\"div\", \"lab-grid\");\n    grid.appendChild(labPositionSizer());\n    grid.appendChild(labRRPlanner());\n    grid.appendChild(labOutcomeR());\n    grid.appendChild(labDrawdown());\n    root.appendChild(grid);\n    root.appendChild(el(\"p\", \"lab-note\", \"Pip values vary by pair — EUR/USD ≈ $10 per standard lot, USD/JPY and others differ. Always confirm with your broker.\"));\n  }\n\n  function labPositionSizer() {\n    const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n    c.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">⚖️</span><div><h3>Position Sizer</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">Net Liquidation × %Risk ÷ (Stop × $/pip)</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tool-in\">\n        <label>Account balance ($)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-bal\" value=\"1000\" min=\"0\" step=\"50\"></label>\n        <label>Risk per trade (%)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-risk\" value=\"1\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" step=\"0.1\"></label>\n        <label>Stop loss (pips)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-stop\" value=\"20\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\"></label>\n        <label>Pip value / std lot ($)<input type=\"number\" id=\"ps-pip\" value=\"10\" min=\"0\" step=\"0.1\"></label>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"ps-result\"><span class=\"dim\">Enter your numbers — the answer updates live</span></div>`;\n    const upd = () => {\n      const b = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-bal\").value || 0;\n      const r = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-risk\").value || 0;\n      const s = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-stop\").value || 0;\n      const p = +c.querySelector(\"#ps-pip\").value || 0;\n      const risk$ = b * r / 100;\n      const lots = (s > 0 && p > 0) ? risk$ / (s * p) : 0;\n      const res = c.querySelector(\"#ps-result\");\n      if (!risk$ || !lots) { res.innerHTML = \"<span class='dim'>Enter your numbers above</span>\"; return; }\n      res.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"out-big\">$${risk$.toFixed(2)} <small>USD at risk</small></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Standard lots</span><b>${lots.toFixed(2)}</b></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Mini lots</span><b>${(lots * 10).toFixed(1)}</b></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Micro lots (contracts)</span><b>${Math.round(lots * 100)}</b></div>`;\n    };\n    c.querySelectorAll(\"input\").forEach(i => i.addEventListener(\"input\", upd));\n    upd();\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  function labRRPlanner() {\n    const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n    c.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">🎯</span><div><h3>R:R Planner</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">How many R is your target worth?</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tool-in\">\n        <label>Entry price<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-entry\" value=\"1.1000\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Stop loss<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-stop\" value=\"1.0900\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Take profit<input type=\"number\" id=\"rr-target\" value=\"1.1300\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Direction<select id=\"rr-side\"><option value=\"long\">Long (buy)</option><option value=\"short\">Short (sell)</option></select></label>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"rr-result\"><span class=\"dim\">Enter your prices — the answer updates live</span></div>`;\n    const upd = () => {\n      const e = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-entry\").value || 0;\n      const s = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-stop\").value || 0;\n      const t = +c.querySelector(\"#rr-target\").value || 0;\n      const side = c.querySelector(\"#rr-side\").value;\n      const R = Math.abs(e - s);\n      const rr = R > 0 ? Math.abs(t - e) / R : 0;\n      const res = c.querySelector(\"#rr-result\");\n      if (!R || !e) { res.innerHTML = \"<span class='dim'>Enter your prices above</span>\"; return; }\n      const good = side === \"long\" ? t > e : t < e;\n      res.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"out-big ${good ? \"\" : \"warn\"}\">1 : ${rr.toFixed(2)} <small>reward to risk</small></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>1R distance</span><b>${R.toFixed(4)}</b></div>\n        ${good ? \"\" : \"<div class='warn-note'>Target sits on the wrong side of entry — flip direction or move the target.</div>\"}`;\n    };\n    c.querySelectorAll(\"input,select\").forEach(i => i.addEventListener(\"input\", upd));\n    upd();\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  function labOutcomeR() {\n    const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n    c.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">📊</span><div><h3>Trade Outcome → R</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">Measure the trade in R, not money</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tool-in\">\n        <label>Entry price<input type=\"number\" id=\"ro-entry\" value=\"1.1000\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Exit price<input type=\"number\" id=\"ro-exit\" value=\"1.1200\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Stop loss<input type=\"number\" id=\"ro-stop\" value=\"1.0900\" step=\"0.0001\"></label>\n        <label>Direction<select id=\"ro-side\"><option value=\"long\">Long (buy)</option><option value=\"short\">Short (sell)</option></select></label>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"ro-result\"><span class=\"dim\">Enter your prices — the answer updates live</span></div>`;\n    const upd = () => {\n      const e = +c.querySelector(\"#ro-entry\").value || 0;\n      const x = +c.querySelector(\"#ro-exit\").value || 0;\n      const s = +c.querySelector(\"#ro-stop\").value || 0;\n      const side = c.querySelector(\"#ro-side\").value;\n      const R = Math.abs(e - s);\n      const res = c.querySelector(\"#ro-result\");\n      if (!R || !e) { res.innerHTML = \"<span class='dim'>Enter your prices above</span>\"; return; }\n      const move = side === \"long\" ? x - e : e - x;\n      const r = move / R;\n      const cls = r > 0 ? \"good\" : r < 0 ? \"warn\" : \"\";\n      const tag = r >= 1 ? \"excellent\" : r > 0 ? \"profit\" : \"loss\";\n      res.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"out-big ${cls}\">${r >= 0 ? \"+\" : \"\"}${r.toFixed(2)}R <small>${tag}</small></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>1R distance</span><b>${R.toFixed(4)}</b></div>\n        ${r < 0 ? \"<div class='warn-note'>In plan, inside rules — a loss of ≤1R is a perfectly managed trade.</div>\" : \"\"}`;\n    };\n    c.querySelectorAll(\"input,select\").forEach(i => i.addEventListener(\"input\", upd));\n    upd();\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  function labDrawdown() {\n    const c = el(\"div\", \"tool-card\");\n    c.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">🕳️</span><div><h3>Drawdown Recovery</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">What you must gain just to get back to even</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tool-in\">\n        <label>Drawdown (%)\n          <select id=\"dd-val\">\n            ${[10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60].map(v => `<option value=\"${v}\" ${v === 50 ? \"selected\" : \"\"}>${v}%</option>`).join(\"\")}\n          </select>\n        </label>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tool-result\" id=\"dd-result\"><span class=\"dim\">Select a drawdown</span></div>`;\n    const upd = () => {\n      const v = +c.querySelector(\"#dd-val\").value || 0;\n      const need = v / (100 - v) * 100;\n      const res = c.querySelector(\"#dd-result\");\n      res.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"out-big ${v >= 50 ? \"warn\" : \"\"}\">${need.toFixed(1)}% <small>gain needed to recover</small></div>\n        <div class=\"out-row\"><span>Your account after drawdown</span><b>${(100 - v).toFixed(0)}% of starting</b></div>\n        ${v >= 50 ? \"<div class='warn-note'>Below 50% it becomes extremely hard to recover — protect the account before it gets here.\" : \"\"}\n        <div class=\"out-hint\">A 50% loss needs a 100% gain. That's why position size must shrink with the account.</div>`;\n    };\n    c.querySelector(\"#dd-val\").addEventListener(\"change\", upd);\n    upd();\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  /* ============================================================\n     CERTIFICATE\n     ============================================================ */","allowMultiple":false},{"oldString":"    if (view === \"map\") renderMap(viewEl);\n    else if (view === \"lesson\") renderLesson(viewEl, parseInt(parts[1], 10), parts[2] ? parseInt(parts[2], 10) : null);","newString":"    if (view === \"map\") renderMap(viewEl);\n    else if (view === \"lab\") renderLab(viewEl);\n    else if (view === \"lesson\") renderLesson(viewEl, parseInt(parts[1], 10), parts[2] ? parseInt(parts[2], 10) : null);","allowMultiple":false}]}},{"kind":"text","text":"\nNow the nav link and the Laboratory styling:"},{"kind":"ad","id":"p5-409297b5","ad":{"adText":"Your tool schema matters more than your model. Clear definitions took every one of 14 models to 100% accuracy. See the benchmark.","title":"Benchmark Report: Why Your MCP Tools Fail ","cta":"Read Now","url":"https://www.arcade.dev/white-papers/mcp-tool-evaluation-benchmark/","favicon":"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.arcade.dev&sz=64","clickUrl":"https://api.trygravity.ai/track/click?p=gAAAAABqdJN_dr8pknK_SFKWmOLYyyqeWllEnC3IY0LYWex6kE2ozpaOuoRd7y-lPhSttxO_R0cCBQdaS44y8JW0TYjaV4F7G0F_T4FbE-5PRfUMWb-xS7FYC_8744XfsFQ24dwkUjUkcFUbAb5Vu-OC-mot-raVzImzdEWtZiwSmhhzr8OyS4bxzdblbv5OImEhR-pVR-BsIJBQDLCmGOSRIkJxEz6yjJH0ob7buZoqbaiWCsE4-1Y-eriM3WKwNXeTg9V1wJIi_UDbAN4XnjkWvhjji5nUeZjAWYjNyCBAN8EG_fXKY56gbTw6YSoIrynQbjLnB_nDD39zYIxCwzjhULXAVDJt3de5SJHvZPNHLrHdIEiOkoLg1SqYV-n1g2TtOhwHU1NCqdqw8tttmDvlYuNwIs6cFAQwM2osZmOGuZFTgg1lgHpynvB9YiS7xz54DVjMdDnhSRaqXVc8lJKfqxmwVLmOeuFtS36Z9oxW0dpgDvzvvpcRTAV8GaP0g-o2Leb4gJFHa7wJcGWq40qpJXuqKU5CVkXLafYN2nevUKW-KbvCpyduajmJ7GG2402Z9McUBQsjG4e0KXO4B6C4FoedwML2_OwoNrtEjtQQMs0uW3UMgfGUmXxktGGMflM0yIWx6ZJpQ6CCSCJAdQOC4MbMfIWj_TlqCSgvQPcOLKXYa8wfVjy28W9AUbK0maANl2jwjGeLbVfXZ8n2xM6E2jLChXVwnioonPi0-Ll2bDWc2h23Rz6e1fLEJVqYUw0eKxwi55V1cL6Cq2zKAkuuKgML3nKSAce2X58G109sDB9roHuaF5HgXAceYgF60eMHPaD0KrwbscO7oJGaH3vPFbGTlnguz-sE9IwaN1KJeAmoS4QlH_dRrjOscdyBTd3cNo0_6kY1Ul4ogW9vyRkBwUrOex6O_UJM1xvVWbiCEXJ7gR2EdyzvaTuV78i2oLfigsXW0VP5qdt80KtzD--_DILCJHGzDp25VFHZ5vfS_