nswer keys, then draft keys for Ch 3-13 chapter by chapter\n2. Extract-then-hide: keep slide assets out of public URLs until Phase 2 gating\n3. Phase 2: Firebase auth + admin access-granting + PayFast checkout links\n4. Phase 2/3: Journal, Experience scenarios (Ch 4/5/9 engines), Laboratory\n\n## 8. Showcase / Free Trial Mode (conversion engine) 🎟️\n\n**Idea:** anyone can see the whole academy (all 13 chapters on the journey map) but cannot enter any content. Entering Chapter 1 requires purchase.\n\n**Approved design (my recommendation):**\n- **Catalog mode (free, no account):** full journey map renders - every chapter title, focus, slide count visible with gold lock icons\n- **Sneak peek:** Chapter 1's first 3 slides viewable free (the strongest conversion lever in education - \"watch the first lesson free\")\n- Every locked chapter shows a gold **\"Purchase to unlock\"** CTA\n- Access mode flag in state: `mode: \"catalog\" | \"student\"` - students (post-purchase) get full access\n- Real enforcement requires Phase 2 (accounts); the showcase UI ships now, hard gating with Phase 2\n\n## 9. Course Modules Roadmap (the Academy expansion) 🏫\n\nThe OS engine is course-agnostic (one CHAPTERS array per course), so new modules reuse 100% of the platform: dashboard, journey, quizzes, laboratory, ranks, certificates.\n\n| Module | Status | Notes |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| **RFX Full Course** (Forex) | Built | 13 chapters, 741 slides |\n| **Reality FX: Crypto** | Future | 8-12 chapters, created from scratch |\n| **Reality FX: Commodities** | Future | Gold, oil, grains - natural follow-on |\n| **Reality FX: Stocks** | Future | Extends the Chapter 12 foundation |\n| **Reality FX: Derivatives** | Future | Options, futures, CFDs - advanced tier |\n\nOrder suggestion: Crypto & Commodities first (closest to forex knowledge), then Stocks, then Derivatives. Each module ships chapter by chapter - content creation by me + Leeroy's expertise and verification.\n\n## 10. Native Slide Rebuild (premium content upgrade) 🎨\n\n**Problem:** extracted slides carry Nearpod branding and don't match the premium gold/dark theme.\n\n**Plan (approved direction, chapter-by-chapter):**\n1. OCR all 741 slides to recover their text (slides are images - OCR is the reliable extraction path)\n2. Rebuild each slide as a native OS card - dark background, gold elements, the site's typography\n3. Weave in Quality-Pass improvements as each chapter is rebuilt\n4. Start with Chapter 1 (22 slides) as the proof, then proceed chapter by chapter\n\nNative rebuild also solves watermark/DRM concerns long-term: content becomes structured data, not images.","allowMultiple":false}]}},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"},{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p14-8dc92781","text":"The blueprint is updated with all three strategic directions. Now let me write the final response covering:\n\n1. **Free trial idea** — my take + what I've designed\n2. **Course modules** — yes, the engine supports it\n3. **Slide recreation** — yes, with the honest OCR path\n4. The two fixes done (spacing + icons) + the bonus bug I found and fixed (dashboard truncation!)\n\nThen suggest_prompts.\n\nKeep it energetic but organized. The user asked \"let me know\" on the slide recreation — so give a clear recommendation and ask for green light on OCR.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"Done — the two polish fixes are live, and I found + fixed a hidden bug along the way. And the blueprint now carries all three of your big ideas. Here's the full picture:\n\n## ✅ The quick fixes (live in your Preview now)\n\n1. **Spacing fixed** — the Continue button and the progress ring now breathe apart properly\n2. **Emojis → premium gold icons** — the dashboard's stat cards and \"coming soon\" chips now use the same refined gold line-icon style as your main site (trophy, document, badge, flame, flask, robot, pen)\n3. **Bonus bug I caught:** the dashboard was silently cutting off after the stats — the rank card, certificate teaser, and name box were never rendering. It's now complete, and it looks sharp.\n\n## 🎟️ On the free-trial idea — my honest take: **brilliant, with one upgrade**\n\nShowing the *whole catalog* while gating entry is smart — it builds desire (\"look what's waiting behind these 13 doors\"). But here's the upgrade that'll convert hardest: **let them see the first 3 slides of Chapter 1 for free.** The strongest sales lever in all of education is \"watch the first lesson free\" — once a skeptical visitor *tastes* the quality, \"forex isn't for me\" melts into \"how do I get the rest?\" Your model stays: everything else stays gold-locked with a **Purchase to unlock** CTA. I've designed it as a **Catalog Mode** in the blueprint — free visitors get the full journey map with locks, students get everything. The showcase UI can ship now; the hard security gate lands with Phase 2 accounts.\n\n## 🏫 On the 5-module academy — **absolutely, and the engine is already built for it**\n\nThis is the blueprint's \"Academy Expansion\" coming to life. The OS doesn't care what the subject is — same dashboard, journey, quizzes, laboratory, ranks, certificates, just a new course file. So: **RFX Full Course (done) → Crypto → Commodities → Stocks → Derivatives**, each 8–12 chapters, created from scratch with the same QC treatment you just saw. Crypto and Commodities first (closest to your existing material), Stocks next (Chapter 12 already plants the seed), Derivatives last as the advanced tier. It'll take time — but every module makes the other four more valuable. This is how a trading school becomes *the* trading school.\n\n## 🎨 On rebuilding the slides — **yes, this is the right endgame, and here's the honest path**\n\nYou're 100% right: Nearpod branding on the slides cheapens the premium feel, and your students deserve the gold/dark treatment. Here's the one honest constraint: **the slides are images, and I can't see images** — so to recreate the text, the reliable path is **OCR** (