loop:\n\n```js\n(() => {\n  window._ocr = { results: {}, done: 0, total: 8, slides: [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,22] };\n  (async () => {\n    for (const n of window._ocr.slides) {\n      try {\n        const r = await Tesseract.recognize('/os/assets/ocr-hi/ch1/slide-' + String(n).padStart(2,'0') + '.png', 'eng');\n        window._ocr.results[n] = r.data.text;\n      } catch (e) { window._ocr.results[n] = 'ERROR: ' + e.message; }\n      window._ocr.done++;\n    }\n    window._ocr.finished = true;\n  })();\n  return 'started';\n})()\n```\n\nThen poll with evaluate: `window._ocr` — but each poll evaluate itself takes <1s (just reads object). The OCR runs in background. \n\nOne risk: does the page keep processing while preview_evaluate is idle? The webview is alive; timers/promises run. Earlier the 10s limit was on a single awaited expression. Detached async loops should continue.\n\nAlso the first Tesseract.recognize warms up (downloads core/traineddata) — takes ~5-10s but it's in the background loop now, fine.\n\nLet me start it.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"OCR exceeds the single-call limit — I'll run it as a background batch and poll for results:"},{"kind":"tool","id":"13p-u7Vb7ew","toolName":"preview_evaluate","input":{"expression":"(() => {\n  window._ocr = { results: {}, done: 0, total: 8, slides: [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,22], finished: false };\n  (async () => {\n    for (const n of window._ocr.slides) {\n      try {\n        const r = await Tesseract.recognize('/os/assets/ocr-hi/ch1/slide-' + String(n).padStart(2, '0') + '.png', 'eng', { logger: () => {} });\n        window._ocr.results[n] = r.data.text;\n      } catch (e) { window._ocr.results[n] = 'ERROR: ' + e.message; }\n      window._ocr.done++;\n    }\n    window._ocr.finished = true;\n  })();\n  return 'batch started';\n})()"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"13qXyT5cPfg","toolName":"preview_evaluate","input":{"expression":"(() => { const o = window._ocr; return { done: o.done, total: o.total, finished: o.fi