Retail Traders — individual traders trading own equity\" + \"Types of equity traders: Scalping — profiting off small price changes, fast, multiple positions\"\n- **Slide 6:** \"Momentum Trading — stocks moving significantly in one direction with high volume (trend)\" + \"Technical Traders — charts and graphs, convergence/divergence signals\" + \"Fundamental Trading — corporate events, earnings reports, splits, acquisitions\" + \"Swing Trading — hold positions longer than a day\" (OCR garbled: \"Fiindamantal tradare wwhn hanlAd thair nncitinne Innnar than a\" = \"Fundamental traders who hold their positions longer than a day\")\n- **Slide 7:** \"Day traders — pick a side at the beginning of the day, act on bias, close by end of day, don't hold overnight\" + \"Position traders — trades lasting weeks, months, or years; fundamental themes predominant\" + \"Fundamental traders — most fundamentalists are really swing trading since changes in corporate fundamentals take days/weeks to produce price movement sufficient for the trader to claim a reasonable profit\"\n- **Slide 22:** \"What resonates with scalping\" — wait, slide 22 OCR shows \"What resonates with scalping\" — that's odd; slide 21 was the scalping quiz question. Slide 22 is the last page (\"22/22\"). The OCR may have caught a fragment. Slide 22 is likely the final poll or closing slide. From the original extraction, slide 22 was just the last page marker (no content). The quiz's last question \"What resonates with scalping\" was slide 21. So slide 22 = closing/end slide — probably \"End of Chapter 1\" or the self-assessment. I'll make slide 22 a closing card: \"End of Chapter 1 — you're on your way. Reflect and continue to the quiz.\" Actually the finish flow handles the quiz + poll. Slide 22 can be a simple \"Chapter 1 complete — well done\" closing card.\n\nAlso slides 8-10 (polls) — I know their content from the original extraction:\n- Slide 8: Poll \"What kind of trader do you want to be... Technical Trader / Fundamental Trader / Swing Trader / Scalper\"\n- Slide 9: Poll (empty marker)\n- Slide 10: Poll \"How do you feel you've performed this chapter\" — but that's the end-of-chapter self-assessment which appears at slide 10?? Wait, in the original extraction: slide 10 \"How do you feel like you've performed this chapter\" poll, and the quiz at 11-21, then 22 end. So the self-assessment poll appears mid-chapter at slide 10 (odd placement in the original, but it's their design — it was likely a template artifact). In the OS, the finish flow already has the poll. For native slides 8-10, I'll render them as nice poll-style cards: slide 8 = \"Which trader are you?\" interactive-ish (or just presented), slide 9 = ??? (empty), slide 10 = self-assessment prompt (already covered at finish — I'll present it as a reflection card, maybe skip duplicating interactivity).\n\nActually — for the native rebuild of slides 8-10, I can make slide 8 an interactive \"trader type\" picker that feeds the journal/XP (nice gamification!), and slide 10 a reflection card. But to keep scope sane for this turn: native cards for 1-10 + 22 (rendering content), quiz slides 11-21 keep the interactive quiz. Slide 8 could be interactive (\"pick your trader type\" → stores choice). Let me add that as a small delight: the trader-type poll on slide 8 becomes interactive with a selection that saves to state and shows on the dashboard (e.g., \"Your trader style: Swing Trader\"). That's a lovely touch and uses their real poll content. But it adds complexity — the lesson player's native card system needs to support a \"poll\" card type. Manageable: native cards can have a `kind: 'poll'` with options.\n\nLet me design the native lesson data structure:\n\n```js\n// in CHAPTERS entry for ch1:\nnative: [\n  { t: \"The Forex Market\", sub: \"Focal points in this chapter\", body: [...], bullets: [...], callout: \"...\" },\n  ...\n]\n```\n\nCard fields:\n- eyebrow: small label (e.g., \"Chapter 1 · Slide 2\")\n- title