et me look at the current drawSlide code to modify it precisely. The current code:\n\n```js\nfunction drawSlide(stage) {\n  const ch = session.ch, st = chState(ch.id);\n  const n = session.idx + 1;\n  touch();\n  if (!st.viewed.includes(n)) { st.viewed.push(n); addXp(XP_SLIDE); save(); }\n  const pct = ...;\n  ...\n  const isQuizSlide = ch.quiz && ch.quizSlides.includes(n);\n  const quizQ = isQuizSlide ? ch.quiz[ch.quizSlides.indexOf(n)] : null;\n\n  stage.innerHTML = `\n    <div class=\"stage-frame\">\n      ...\n      <img ...>\n      ...\n    </div>\n    ${quizQ ? quizCard(quizQ) : \"\"}\n    <div class=\"stage-nav\">...</div>`;\n  ...\n  document.getElementById(\"next\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    if (isQuizSlide && ch.quiz) {\n      if (session.answered[n] === undefined) { toast(...); return; }\n    }\n    if (n >= ch.slides) finishChapter(stage);\n    else { session.idx++; drawSlide(stage); }\n  });\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nChanges:\n- After computing isQuizSlide, compute `const native = ch.native ? ch.native[n - 1] : null;`\n- `const isPollSlide = native && native.kind === \"poll\";`\n- Stage innerHTML: replace the stage-frame block with `native ? nativeCard(native, n) : '<div class=\"stage-frame\">...'`\n- Next guard: `if ((isQuizSlide && ch.quiz) || isPollSlide) { if (session.answered[n] === undefined) {...} }`\n\nnativeCard(native, n):\n```js\nfunction nativeCard(native, n) {\n  const chosen = session.answered[n];\n  let opts = \"\";\n  if (native.kind === \"poll\") {\n    opts = `<div class=\"native-poll\">\n      ${native.options.map((o, i) => `<button class=\"native-poll-opt ${chosen === i ? \"sel\" : \"\"}\" data-i=\"${i}\" ${chosen !== undefined ? \"disabled\" : \"\"}>${esc(o)}</button>`).join(\"\")}\n      ${chosen !== undefined ? `<div class=\"quiz-fb good\">Stored — you can change this identity any time.</div>` : \"\"}\n    </div>`;\n  }\n  return `\n    <div class=\"native-card\">\n      ${native.eyebrow ? `<p class=\"quiz-tag\">${esc(native.eyebrow)}</p>` : \"\"}\n      ${native.title ? `<h2 class=\"native-title gold-serif\">${esc(native.title)}</h2>` : \"\"}\n      ${native.lead ? `<p class=\"native-lead\">${esc(native.lead)}</p>` : \"\"}\n      ${(native.body || []).map(p => `<p class=\"native-body\">${esc(p)}</p>`).join(\"\")}\n      ${(native.bullets || []).map(b => `<div class=\"native-bullet\"><span class=\"nb-dot\"></span><p>${esc(b)}</p></div>`).join(\"\")}\n      ${native.example ? `<div class=\"native-example\">${esc(native.example)}</div>` : \"\"}\n      ${native.callout ? `<div class=\"native-callout\">“${esc(native.callout)}”</div>` : \"\"}\n      ${opts}\n    </div>`;\n}\n```\n\nNote: for kind \"close\", style as a finishing card (larger). I can add a class variant: `native-card ${native.kind === \"close\" ? \"native-close\" : \"\"}` and style it centered with the finish-ic 🎓? Let me add a medal icon for close. I'll include an SVG or emoji? The user wants premium — use a gold SVG (ICONS.trophy). Add `native.kind === \"close\" ? '<div class=\"native-close-ic\">' + ICONS.trophy + '</div>' : \"\"`.\n\nDelegated handler for native-poll-opt:\n```js\ndocument.addEventListener(\"click\", e => {\n  const opt = e.target.closest(\".native-poll-opt\");\n  if (!opt || opt.disabled || !session.ch) return;\n  const n = session.idx + 1;\n  if (session.answered[n] !== undefined) return;\n  session.answered[n] = parseInt(opt.dataset.i, 10);\n  S.traderStyle = session.ch.native[n - 1].options[session.answered[n]];\n  save();\n  toast(\"Identity saved — this can evolve\", \"rank\");\n  drawSlide(document.querySelector(\".stage\"));\n});\n```\n\nDashboard: show trader style. In renderDashboard, add near the name-box or in hero. I'll add a small chip in the hero under the CTA:\n```js\n${S.traderStyle ? `<div class=\"style-chip\">${ICONS.check} Your style: <b>${esc(S.traderStyle)}</b></div>` : \"\"}\n```\nPlace it after the dash-cta div.\n\nCSS for native cards + style chip. Let me write those.\n\nOne more thing — the resume logic: when a user returns to ch1 (native slides), resume at first unviewed. Fine.\n\nAlso the \"close\" slide (22) — after it, next → finishChapter. Good.\n\nNow let me also double check: slide numbers for native array — native[0] = slide 1, ..., native[9] = slide 10, native[10] = slide 22 (close). Wait — my array has 11 entries: slides 1-10, then close. Let me count: \n1. opener (slide 1)\n2. FX market (slide 2)\n3. Both sides (slide 3)\n4. players (slide 4)\n5. institutional vs retail (slide 5)\n6. styles (slide 6)\n7. day & position (slide 7)\n8. poll (slide 8)\n9. open mind (slide 9)\n10. mid-chapter reflection (slide 10)\n11. close (slide 22)!\n\nnative[n-1] for n=22 → native[21] → undefined! The close card is at index 10 (slide 11) but I need it at index 21 (slide 22). Mismatch!\n\nFix: the close card must be at index 21 in the array (22nd entry) — but quiz slides 11-21 have no native cards. So I need the array to have 22 entries with nulls for slides 11-21. Or handle the close specially. Cleaner: make the native array exactly 22 entries: entries 0-9 (slides 1-10), entries 10-20 = null (quiz slides 11-21), entry 21 = close card. Let me restructure: after the reflection card (index 9), insert 11 nulls, then the close card. Actually quiz slides still need the image display (which is the default when native[n-1] is null) — good.\n\nLet me fix data.js: add `null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null,` (11 nulls) between index 9 and the close card. Wait — index 9 is slide 10, then slides 11-21 are indices 10-20 (11 entries, null), then index 21 = slide 22 close. Yes.\n\nLet me edit data.js to insert the nulls.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"Now the engine. First, fixing the native array indexing — the close card must sit at slide 22's position (quiz slides 11–21 stay as images):"},{"kind":"tool","id":"13zS2UZglG0","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/js/data.js","rep