ERS — before slidePath). I'll add after QUOTE (line 33).\n\nThe style chapter guides reference chapter ids: \n- Scalper: 4 (Candlesticks), 5 (Market Movement), 9 (Market Orders), 10 (Technical Indicators)\n- Day: 4, 5, 9, 7, 6\n- Swing: 3 (Fundamental), 5, 11 (Market Cycle), 8 (Pairs), 7\n- Position: 3, 11, 8, 12 (Stock Market), 6\n\nEach guide entry: { id, why }.\n\nLet me write STYLES:\n\n```js\nconst STYLES = {\n  scalper: {\n    key: \"scalper\", name: \"Scalper\", icon: \"⚡\",\n    tagline: \"Seconds to minutes — speed is your edge.\",\n    profile: \"Scalping is sprinting: trades measured in seconds to minutes, dozens of entries a day, each one fighting for a few pips. You live on the smallest timeframes — 1m to 5m — where liquidity, spread and execution speed matter more than any indicator.\",\n    edge: [\n      \"Reads price structure and momentum faster than any other style\",\n      \"Compounds small wins daily — no waiting for the 'big move'\",\n      \"20 decisions a day is 20 reps a day: discipline built in volume\"\n    ],\n    watch: [\n      \"Spread + commission are your first costs — they can silently eat a third of a scalp edge\",\n      \"Trading quiet hours — no volatility, no scalp. Know when the market is asleep\",\n      \"The 10th trade of the day is rarely as clean as the 1st — fatigue is a real risk factor\"\n    ],\n    chapters: [\n      { id: 4, why: \"Candlesticks are your native language — instant reads on 1m–5m\" },\n      { id: 5, why: \"Micro structure: where support/resistance lives in your timeframe\" },\n      { id: 9, why: \"Market orders — your execution precision decides your edge\" },\n      { id: 10, why: \"Momentum & volatility indicators that time your entries\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  day: {\n    key: \"day\", name: \"Day Trader\", icon: \"🌅\",\n    tagline: \"One day, one plan — flat before the close.\",\n    profile: \"Day trading is a daily campaign: form a bias at the open, trade it through the session, and close everything flat before the close. No overnight risk, no gaps — your P&L is decided inside a single day.\",\n    edge: [\n      \"Trades daily volatility without ever carrying overnight risk\",\n      \"Every day is a clean slate — losses stay inside their day\",\n      \"Leverages the two highest-liquidity windows: the open and the close\"\n    ],\n    watch: [\n      \"The open is emotional — a bias without a plan becomes a gamble\",\n      \"Midday chop: quiet hours produce the worst fills and the sloppiest trades\",\n      \"'One more hour' on a losing position — the flat-by-close rule exists for a reason\"\n    ],\n    chapters: [\n      { id: 4, why: \"Candles set your intraday entries and exits\" },\n      { id: 5, why: \"Daily structure gives your morning bias its direction\" },\n      { id: 9, why: \"Order types executed at the right moment = your session\" },\n      { id: 7, why: \"Risk management is your daily survival kit\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  swing: {\n    key: \"swing\", name: \"Swing Trader\", icon: \"⛰️\",\n    tagline: \"Days to weeks — let the market come to you.\",\n    profile: \"Swing trading is chess, not sprinting: positions held for days to weeks, riding the structure of higher timeframes — 1H, 4H and daily. You let the market come to your levels, and patience is the edge other styles can't copy.\",\n    edge: [\n      \"Trades with the daily trend instead of fighting intraday noise\",\n      \"Needs only a few quality setups a month — quality over frequency\",\n      \"Fills are forgiving — you don't pay for the exact tick\"\n    ],\n    watch: [\n      \"Overnight and weekend gaps can punish a perfect setup — size for them\",\n      \"Fighting the daily trend to catch a 'cheap' retracement\",\n      \"Position size creeping up on 'sure things' — the monthly P&L is what matters\"\n    ],\n    chapters: [\n      { id: 3, why: \"Fundamentals are the fuel your multi-day moves run on\" },\n      { id: 5, why: \"Trends, support and resistance are your playground\" },\n      { id: 11, why: \"The market cycle tells you which phase your setup sits in\" },\n      { id: 8, why: \"Choosing the right pairs for multi-day structure\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  position: {\n    key: \"position\", name: \"Position Trader\", icon: \"🏔️\",\n    tagline: \"Weeks to years — trade the theme, not the noise.\",\n    profile: \"Position trading is the long game: positions held for weeks, months, even years, built on fundamental themes rather than chart noise. You think in quarters, not candles — and your account compounds on conviction.\",\n    edge: [\n      \"Profits from the big themes impatient traders abandon\",\n      \"Time in the market beats timing the market\",\n      \"Lowest stress of all styles — decisions are measured in weeks\"\n    ],\n    watch: [\n      \"Every thesis needs an exit trigger — 'it'll recover' is not a plan\",\n      \"Drawdown feels different over months — size so you can hold\",\n      \"Stay current: one news event can invalidate the whole theme\"\n    ],\n    chapters: [\n      { id: 3, why: \"Fundamental analysis is the engine of every position\" },\n      { id: 11, why: \"The cycle tells you where the theme is heading\" },\n      { id: 8, why: \"Cross-asset pairs match your multi-week horizon\" },\n      { id: 12, why: \"The stock market broadens your long-term universe\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  general: {\n    key: \"general\", name: \"Explorer\", icon: \"🧭\",\n    tagline: \"Still discovering your edge — that's exactly right.\",\n    profile: \"You haven't settled on a style yet — and Chapter 1 says that's the correct first position. The OS will show you each style's lens as you go, and your analytics will help you see which one your decisions naturally favour.\",\n    edge: [\"Open-minded — not yet locked into one approach\", \"Learning what actually fits before committing\", \"The market will help you choose — and you can change anytime\"],\n    watch: [\"Don't force a style to fit — let your data reveal it\", \"Avoid collecting styles without mastering one\", \"Stay curious through every chapter — especially the ones that feel 'not for you'\"],\n    chapters: [\n      { id: 2, why: \"The language of trading — the foundation everything builds on\" },\n      { id: 4, why: \"Candlesticks — the first skill every style shares\" },\n      { id: 6, why: \"Psychology — your behaviour will reveal your natural style\" }\n    ]\n  }\n};\n```\n\nHmm — one consideration: the icons here are emojis (⚡🌅⛰️🏔️🧭). The user wanted smooth icons. For the style icons, using emojis in the OS... the nav uses emojis, so it's consistent-ish. But to be premium, I could use small SVG paths per style. Let me use minimal SVG paths in data.js — they'll render gold via `color: var(--accent-gold)`. Actually — ICONS in os.js are SVGs. For STYLES in data.js, I can include `icon` as an SVG path string and os.js wraps it via ICON(). That keeps it gold and smooth. Let me do that:\n\n- scalper: lightning bolt `<path d=\"M13 2L4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6l1-8z\"/>`\n- day: sun `<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/><path d=\"M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4\"/>`\n- swing: waves/mountain — use a wave: `<path d=\"M2 12c2.5-4 5-4 7.5 0s5 4 7.5 0 3-2 3-2\"/>` hmm. Use a mountain: `<path d=\"M3 20L10 6l4 8 3-5 4 11H3z\"/>`\n- position: hourglass or globe — globe: `<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M3 12h18M12 3c3 3.5 3 14 0 18M12 3c-3 3.5-3 14 0 18\"/>` (globe lines)\n- general/explorer: compass: `<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M15.5 8.5l-2 5-5 2 2-5 5-2z\"/>`\n\nGood. In STYLES I'll store `icon` as the path string; os.js does `ICON(STYLES[k].icon)`.\n\nNow the poll options update: change to [\"Scalper\", \"Day Trader\", \"Swing Trader\", \"Position Trader\"]. Wait — the poll sub says \"Choose what resonates today.\" Fine.\n\nNote: existing stored traderStyle values (\"Technical Trader\", \"Fundamental Trader\", \"Swing Trader\") — \"Swing Trader\" still works. \"Technical Trader\" → no profile → general fallback. Good.\n\nPer-style notes on native cards. Structure: `styles: { scalper: \"…\", day: \"…\", swing: \"…\", position: \"…\" }` — plain strings shown as the tailored panel. Optionally `{ note, insight }`. Keep it simple: plain strings.\n\nCards to annotate (ch1 native indices):\n- index 3 (slide 4, \"The Traders You'll Meet\")\n- index 5 (slide 6, \"Momentum, Technical, Fundamental, Swing\")\n- index 6 (slide 7, \"Day Traders & Position Traders\")\n- index 8 (slide 9, \"Keep an Open Mind\")\n\nNow os.js changes:\n\n1. Helpers:\n```js\nfunction styleKey() {\n  if (!S.traderStyle) return null;\n  const k = S.traderStyle.toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+trader$/, \"\").trim();\n  return STYLES[k] ? k : \"general\";\n}\nfunction styleProfile() { return S.traderStyle ? STYLES[styleKey()] || STYLES.general : null; }\n```\n\n2. Dashboard style card. Replace:\n```js\n${S.traderStyle ? `<div class=\"style-chip\">${ICONS.check} Trader style: <b>${esc(S.traderStyle)}</b></div>` : \"\"}\n```\nwith a style-card:\n```js\n${styleCardHtml()}\n```\nwhere styleCardHtml returns either the profile card (if style) or the prompt card. But the buttons need listeners. Better: build it as a separate element appended after dash-hero. Let me restructure: after the hero (and before stats), append the style-card element with listeners.\n\nActually simpler: keep it inside dash-hero inner (below dash-cta), and add listeners via querySelector on the root. Let me write a `styleCard()` builder:\n\n```js\nfunction styleCard() {\n  const prof = styleProfile();\n  const card = el(\"div\", \"style-card\");\n  if (!prof) {\n    card.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"style-card-ic\">${ICON(STYLES.general.icon)}</div>\n      <div class=\"style-card-body\">\n        <p class=\"quiz-tag\">Your trader identity</p>\n        <h3 class=\"gold-serif\">What kind of trader are you becoming?</h3>\n        <p>Take the identity question in Chapter 1 — the OS then tailors lessons, insights and focus areas to your style. You can change it any time.</p>\n        <div class=\"style-card-actions\"><button class=\"btn-ghost\" data-style-go=\"1/8\">Find my style</button></div>\n      </div>`;\n  } else {\n    card.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"style-card-ic\">${ICON(prof.icon)}</div>\n      <div class=\"style-card-body\">\n        <p class=\"quiz-tag\">Your trader identity · adaptive</p>\n        <h3 class=\"gold-serif\">${esc(prof.name)}</h3>\n        <p class=\"style-tagline\">${esc(prof.tagline)}</p>\n        <div class=\"style-card-actions\">\n          <button class=\"btn-ghost\" data-style-go=\"path\">Your path</button>\n          <button class=\"btn-ghost\" data-style-go=\"change\">Change style</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>`;\n  }\n  const go = card.querySelector(\"[data-style-go]\");\n  if (go) go.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    if (go.dataset.styleGo === \"path\") location.hash = \"#/path\";\n    else if (go.dataset.styleGo === \"change\") location.hash = \"#/path\";\n    else location.hash = \"#/lesson/\" + go.dataset.styleGo;\n  });\n  return card;\n}\n```\nHmm \"change\" → same as path (the picker lives there). Simplify: two buttons \"Your path & change style\" — one button \"Shape your path\". Let me do one button: \"Shape your path\" → #/path. And in the empty state: \"Find my style\" → #/lesson/1/8.\n\n3. renderPath view:\n\n```js\nfunction renderPath(root) {\n  const prof = styleProfile() || STYLES.general;\n  root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"page-head\", `\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Your Path · adaptive learning</p>\n    <h2>Your trader identity shapes what you read</h2>\n    <p class=\"page-sub\">Every style trades the same market differently. The OS weaves your style's lens into the lessons you open — so you learn the concepts through the eyes of the trader you're becoming.</p>`));\n\n  // Profile card\n  const profileCard = el(\"div\", \"tool-card path-profile\");\n  profileCard.innerHTML = `\n    <div class=\"path-identity\">\n      <div class=\"style-card-ic big\">${ICON(prof.icon)}</div>\n      <div>\n        <p class=\"quiz-tag\">Current identity${S.traderStyle ? \"\" : \" · not chosen yet\"}</p>\n        <h3 class=\"gold-serif\">${esc(prof.name)}</h3>\n        <p class=\"style-tagline\">${esc(prof.tagline)}</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"path-profile-text\">${esc(prof.profile)}</p>\n    <div class=\"path-timeframe\"><span class=\"ni-ic\">🕐</span> <b>Timeframe:</b> ${esc(prof.timeframe || \"All timeframes as you explore\")}</div>`;\n  root.appendChild(profileCard);\n\n  // Edge & watch\n  const duo = el(\"div\", \"lab-grid\");\n  duo.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"tool-card\", `\n    <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">${ICONS.trophy}</span><div><h3>Your edge</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">What makes this style win</p></div></div>\n    ${prof.edge.map(t => `<div class=\"out-row\"><span>${esc(t)}</span></div>`).join(\"\")}`));\n  duo.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"tool-card\", `\n    <div class=\"tool-head\"><span class=\"tool-ic\">${ICONS.sparkle}</span><div><h3>Watch these</h3><p class=\"tool-sub\">The traps that take this style down</p></div></div>\n    ${prof.watch.map(t => `<div class=\"out-row\"><span>${esc(t)}</span></div>`).join(\"\")}`));\n  root.appendChild(duo);\n\n  // Chapter guide\n  root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"panel\", `<h3 class=\"panel-title gold-serif\">Chapters weighted for your path</h3>`));\n  const guide = el(\"div\", \"grade-list\");\n  prof.chapters.forEach(c => {\n    const ch = CHAPTERS.find(x => x.id === c.id);\n    guide.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"grade-row guide-row\", `\n      <span class=\"grade-ch\">${fmt(c.id)} · ${esc(ch ? ch.title : \"\")}</span>\n      <span class=\"grade-why\">${esc(c.why)}</span>\n      <button class=\"btn-ghost guide-go\" data-id=\"${c.id}\">Open</button>`));\n  });\n  root.appendChild(guide);\n  guide.querySelectorAll(\".guide-go\").forEach(b => b.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    const id = +b.dataset.id;\n    if (isUnlocked(CHAPTERS.find(x => x.id === id))) location.hash = \"#/lesson/\" + id;\n    else toast(\"Complete the previous chapters to unlock this one\", \"warn\");\n  }));\n\n  // Change style\n  root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"panel\", `<h3 class=\"panel-title gold-serif\">Change your identity</h3>`));\n  const pick = el(\"div\", \"style-pick\");\n  Object.keys(STYLES).filter(k => k !== \"general\").forEach(k => {\n    const p = STYLES[k];\n    const sel = styleKey() === k;\n    const b = el(\"button\", \"style-pick-opt\" + (sel ? \" sel\" : \"\"), `\n      <span class=\"sp-ic\">${ICON(p.icon)}</span>\n      <span class=\"sp-name\">${esc(p.name)}</span>\n      <span class=\"sp-tag\">${esc(p.tagline)}</span>`);\n    b.addEventListener(\"click\", () => { S.traderStyle = p.name; save(); toast(\"Identity updated — lessons now carry the \" + p.name + \" lens\", \"rank\"); renderPath(root); });\n    pick.appendChild(b);\n  });\n  root.appendChild(pick);\n  root.appendChild(el(\"div\", \"path-note\", `${ICONS.sparkle} <span>Lessons you've already read stay as they are; every card marked “Tailored for you” will carry the ${esc(prof.name)} lens from now on.</span>`));\n}\n```\n\nWait — renderPath(root) re-renders by appending to root — but root is `#view`, and route() clears it before calling. Inside the pick handler, calling renderPath(root) again would append duplicates. Need to clear root first: `root.innerHTML = \"\"; renderPath(root);`. Let me do that.\n\n4. nativeCard tailored panel:\n\nIn nativeCard, add before the closing:\n```js\nconst stKey = styleKey();\nconst styleNote = stKey && native.styles ? native.styles[stKey] : null;\n...\n${styleNote ? `<div class=\"native-style\"><span class=\"ns-badge\">${ICONS.sparkle} Tailored for ${esc(styleProfile().name)}s</span><p>${esc(styleNote)}</p></div>` : \"\"}\n```\nHmm \"Swing Traders\" — pluralization: profile.name + \"s\" → \"Scalpers\", \"Day Traders\", \"Swing Traders\", \"Position Traders\". Works for all four. Good.\n\nAlso the poll feedback: \"Saved — this identity now shows on your dashboard.\" → add \"and tailors your lessons.\" Update that text.\n\nAlso the poll sub text: maybe update \"Choose what resonates today\" — fine as is.\n\n5. buildInsights style gem: at the end of buildInsights:\n```js\nconst prof = styleProfile();\nif (prof) {\n  const next = prof.chapters[0];\n  gems.push({ cls: \"gold\", title: `Your path: ${prof.name}`,\n    body: `Lessons tagged “Tailored for you” now carry the ${prof.name} lens. Next on your path: ${next ? CHAPTERS.find(c => c.id === next.id).title : \"keep exploring\"}.` });\n}\n```\nOrder: maybe push it first (before others) so it's prominent. I'll push at the start after the graded.length check... Actually push it first thing after the empty-state check. Hmm — let me push it right after the graded check so it appears at top:\n\nActually the gems order: currently avgGrade gem first. I'll insert the style gem first so it's the headline. Let me restructure buildInsights to push style gem right after the graded.length===0 early return.\n\n6. Router: add `else if (view === \"path\") renderPath(viewEl);`\n\n7. index.html nav: add after Performance:\n`<a class=\"nav-item\" data-route=\"#/path\"><span class=\"ni-ic\">🧭</span>Your Path</a>`\n\nHmm wait — should nav use emoji 🧭 or a gold SVG? Existing nav items use emojis. Keep 🧭.\n\n8. CSS additions:\n- `.style-card` — a gold-bordered row card (flex, icon left)\n- `.style-card-ic` — gold icon circle\n- `.style-card-ic.big` — larger\n- `.style-tagline` — italic quote font\n- `.style-card-actions`\n- `.native-style` — tailored panel (gold left border, subtle bg)\n- `.ns-badge` — small gold tag\n- `.path-identity` — flex\n- `.path-profile-text`\n- `.path-timeframe`\n- `.guide-row` layout (flex with why text)\n- `.grade-why`\n- `.style-pick` grid\n- `.style-pick-opt` cards\n- `.sp-ic`, `.sp-name`, `.sp-tag`\n- `.path-note`\n- `.style-chip` keep (used elsewhere? only dashboard old spot — I'm replacing with style-card; keep style-chip CSS harmlessly or remove? I'll leave it; no harm. Actually I'll remove usage; CSS can stay.)\n\nLet me look at CSS variables and existing patterns for colors: `--accent-gold`, `--accent-gold-light`, `--accent-gold-dim`, `--glass-border`, `--border-subtle`, `--text-dim`, `--text-muted`, `--font-quote`, `--danger`. Let me check the :root vars and .tool-card, .grade-row, .out-row styles to match.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":"Now I'll build. First the STYLES profiles in data.js (after `QUOTE`, before `CHAPTERS`):"},{"kind":"tool","id":"15cy6PxyOiQ","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"REALITY-FOREX-TRADING-/os/js/data.js","replacements":[{"oldString":"const QUOTE = \"Every lesson is a trade. Every trade is a lesson.\";","newString":"const QUOTE = \"Every lesson is a trade. Every trade is a lesson.\";\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------\n   TRADER STYLES — adaptive learning profiles\n   Each style carries its own lens: identity, edge, traps and a\n   personalized chapter guide. The OS weaves the student's chosen\n   style into the lessons they read, the insights they get, and\n   the path they're guided along.\n   ------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst STYLES = {\n  scalper: {\n    key: \"scalper\", name: \"Scalper\",\n    icon: \"<path d='M13 2L4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6l1-8z'/>\",\n    tagline: \"Seconds to minutes — speed is your edge.\",\n    timeframe: \"1m – 5m charts · positions held seconds to minutes\",\n    profile: \"Scalping is sprinting: trades measured in seconds to minutes, dozens of entries a day, each one fighting for a few pips. You live on the smallest timeframes — 1m to 5m — where liquidity, spread and execution speed matter more than any indicator.\",\n    edge: [\n      \"Reads price structure and momentum faster than any other style\",\n      \"Compounds small wins 